        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-a">A</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ad-revenue/" class="glossary-card-term">Ad Revenue</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The money YouTube pays creators from ads shown on their videos. YouTube keeps 45% and pays creators 55% on long-form content; Shorts use a separate pooled model based on engaged views.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ad-revenue/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ad-suitability-checks/" class="glossary-card-term">Ad Suitability Checks</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's upload and monetization reviews that determine whether a video can earn most ads, limited ads, or no ad earnings. Icons in YouTube Studio show checking, green, yellow, or red status — and results can change after the initial review.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ad-suitability-checks/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/adsense-for-youtube/" class="glossary-card-term">AdSense for YouTube</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Google's payment-account system that receives finalized YouTube earnings, manages tax information, verification, payment methods, thresholds, and monthly payment issuance. Separate from YouTube Analytics, which shows only estimated revenue.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/adsense-for-youtube/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-advanced-features/" class="glossary-card-term">Advanced Features</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A set of YouTube permissions unlocked via phone or ID verification that lets creators upload longer videos, go live, appeal strikes, and access the Community tab. Required before applying to the YouTube Partner Program.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-advanced-features/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-advanced-mode/" class="glossary-card-term">Advanced Mode</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube Studio's expanded analytics view that lets creators dig deeper into metrics, compare multiple data points side by side, and access granular breakdowns not available in the standard dashboard.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-advanced-mode/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-affiliate-marketing/" class="glossary-card-term">Affiliate Marketing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A monetization strategy where creators earn a commission each time a viewer makes a purchase through their unique affiliate link. Commonly used alongside sponsorships in gear reviews and tutorials.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-affiliate-marketing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-algorithm/" class="glossary-card-term">Algorithm</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's recommendation system that analyzes watch time, click-through rate, and satisfaction signals to decide which videos to surface on the homepage, in search, and in suggested content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-algorithm/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ask-me-anything/" class="glossary-card-term">AMA (Ask Me Anything)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video or live stream format where a creator opens the floor for audience questions and answers them in real time or in a dedicated video. A popular community-building and low-prep content type.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ask-me-anything/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ask-studio/" class="glossary-card-term">Ask Studio</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's AI assistant built into YouTube Studio. Helps creators brainstorm video ideas, write titles and descriptions, and get answers about their analytics without leaving the platform.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ask-studio/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/audience-interest/" class="glossary-card-term">Audience Interest</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A relative signal in YouTube Studio's Trends tab estimating how interested a creator's specific audience may be in a topic or search idea, displayed on a Very Low to Very High scale based on 28-day viewing data — a comparison tool, not a guaranteed traffic prediction.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/audience-interest/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-audio-library/" class="glossary-card-term">Audio Library</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's built-in collection of royalty-free music and sound effects available free to all creators through YouTube Studio, usable in videos without triggering copyright claims.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-audio-library/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/auto-dubbing/" class="glossary-card-term">Auto-Dubbing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A free YouTube AI feature that translates a video's spoken audio and attaches a generated voice track in another language to the original upload, expanding reach to international audiences without re-uploading.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/auto-dubbing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/auto-generated-clips/" class="glossary-card-term">Auto-Generated Clips</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube AI feature that scans an existing long-form video and suggests short highlight clips for creators to share, saving time on manual clip selection and cross-platform promotion.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/auto-generated-clips/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/auto-generated-shorts/" class="glossary-card-term">Auto-Generated Shorts</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube AI feature that automatically repurposes segments from an uploaded long-form video into Shorts, helping creators extend content reach without additional filming or editing.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/auto-generated-shorts/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/automatic-chapters/" class="glossary-card-term">Automatic Chapters</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube-generated sections that divide an eligible video into labeled parts without the creator manually adding timestamped chapter titles. Creators can enable, disable, or override them with valid manual timestamps in the description.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/automatic-chapters/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/average-percentage-viewed/" class="glossary-card-term">Average Percentage Viewed (APV)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The average share of a video's total length that viewers watch, expressed as a percentage. A 70% APV means the typical viewer watches seven-tenths of the video before stopping or leaving.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/average-percentage-viewed/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/average-view-duration/" class="glossary-card-term">Average View Duration (AVD)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The average number of minutes viewers spend watching a video. Higher AVD signals strong audience retention and is a key factor in how the YouTube algorithm ranks and recommends content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/average-view-duration/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-b">B</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/b-roll/" class="glossary-card-term">B-Roll</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Supporting footage edited alongside the primary on-camera footage. B-roll covers cuts, illustrates what's being said, and adds visual variety — essential for making talking-head videos more engaging and watchable.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/b-roll/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/blocked-words/" class="glossary-card-term">Blocked Words</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A channel-level YouTube moderation list where creators add words and phrases that trigger holds on matching comments and block matching live chat messages. Applies channel-wide (not per video), held comments can be reviewed for up to 60 days, and approved users bypass the filter entirely.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/blocked-words/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-branding-watermark/" class="glossary-card-term">Branding Watermark</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A small clickable logo or image creators add to the corner of all their videos via YouTube Studio. It typically links to a subscribe prompt and appears as a persistent brand element throughout playback.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-branding-watermark/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/breakout-videos/" class="glossary-card-term">Breakout Videos</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A personalized Trends tab card in YouTube Studio highlighting well-performing content from creators whose channels are similar to yours. Intended as inspiration for ideas, not a public viral chart — the featured videos have no publicly defined view threshold.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/breakout-videos/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/browse-features/" class="glossary-card-term">Browse Features</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The YouTube analytics traffic source that captures impressions and views coming from the homepage and Subscriptions feed. Strong browse performance means YouTube is actively pushing a video to logged-in viewers.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/browse-features/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-burnout/" class="glossary-card-term">Burnout</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A state of chronic exhaustion, creative depletion, or loss of motivation many creators experience after sustained high-output production. Recognizing the signs and building sustainable schedules is a common topic in creator wellbeing.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-burnout/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-c">C</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cta/" class="glossary-card-term">Call to Action (CTA)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A verbal or on-screen prompt asking viewers to take a specific action, such as subscribing, clicking a link, or leaving a comment. Effective CTAs are concise, specific, and placed at moments of peak engagement.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cta/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-cards/" class="glossary-card-term">Cards</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Small interactive notifications that appear during YouTube videos, linking viewers to other videos, playlists, channels, or external URLs. Creators add them in YouTube Studio to direct traffic and extend watch sessions.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-cards/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/casual-viewers/" class="glossary-card-term">Casual Viewers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics audience segment for viewers who returned to a channel at least once per month for one to five months in the past year — between new viewers and regular viewers in loyalty.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/casual-viewers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-category/" class="glossary-card-term">Category</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The content genre assigned to a video in YouTube Studio (e.g., Education, Entertainment, Gaming). Categories help YouTube understand a video's subject and recommend it to viewers likely to enjoy that type of content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-category/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-channel/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator's home on YouTube where all their videos, playlists, community posts, and channel information live. Visitors browse the channel page to subscribe, explore content, and learn more about the creator.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-channel/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-art/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Art</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The banner image displayed at the top of a YouTube channel page. A key branding element, typically 2560×1440 pixels, often including the creator's name, upload schedule, and visual identity.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-art/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-description/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Description</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A text field on a YouTube channel page where creators describe their content, niche, and upload schedule. It's indexed by YouTube search and helps new visitors decide quickly whether to subscribe.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-description/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-keywords/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Keywords</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Tags added in YouTube Studio's channel settings to help YouTube categorize a channel's overall content and connect it with relevant searches. Distinct from individual video tags and applied at the channel level.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-keywords/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/channel-memberships/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Memberships</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A paid subscription feature where viewers pay a monthly fee for perks like exclusive badges, custom emojis, members-only posts, or early access to videos. Requires active YouTube Partner Program membership.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/channel-memberships/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/channel-pages-traffic/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Pages Traffic</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Traffic generated when viewers find and open a video from your YouTube channel page or another creator's channel page — distinct from Browse Features (Home/Subscriptions) and most useful for evaluating intentional audience exploration or collaboration impact.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/channel-pages-traffic/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/channel-permissions/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Permissions</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Settings that control what different team members or managers can do inside a creator's YouTube Studio — from uploading videos to managing comments, editing descriptions, or accessing analytics.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/channel-permissions/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/channel-trailer/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Trailer</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video selected by the creator to appear at the top of the channel Home tab for non-subscribers. YouTube shows it only once per viewer after they watch it — intended to preview the channel and give new visitors a reason to subscribe or keep watching.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/channel-trailer/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/channels-your-audience-watches/" class="glossary-card-term">Channels Your Audience Watches</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics report showing other channels your viewers consistently watched outside your channel over the past 28 days — used to identify audience interests, collaboration candidates, and adjacent creator communities.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/channels-your-audience-watches/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/click-through-rate/" class="glossary-card-term">Click-Through Rate (CTR)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The percentage of YouTube impressions that result in someone clicking to watch a video. A higher CTR means the thumbnail and title are compelling enough to make viewers stop scrolling and watch.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/click-through-rate/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/clickbait/" class="glossary-card-term">Clickbait</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Titles or thumbnails that exaggerate, mislead, or withhold key information to drive clicks but fail to deliver on the implied promise. Clickbait can temporarily inflate CTR while damaging retention and long-term audience trust.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/clickbait/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/closed-captions/" class="glossary-card-term">Closed Captions (CC)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Text overlays synchronized to a video's audio that display dialogue and sounds for viewers who are deaf, hard of hearing, or watching without sound. YouTube auto-generates captions, which creators can edit for accuracy.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/closed-captions/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-collab/" class="glossary-card-term">Collab</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video or live stream produced by two or more creators working together, either appearing in the same video or cross-promoting each other's content. Collabs are a proven strategy for audience cross-pollination and subscriber growth.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-collab/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/comment-moderation/" class="glossary-card-term">Comment Moderation</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's system of settings, review queues, moderator roles, and automated filters for managing who can comment and which comments publish publicly. Includes four moderation levels (None, Basic, Strict, Hold all), channel-default and per-video settings, and a held-comment queue that expires after 60 days.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/comment-moderation/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/collab-remix/" class="glossary-card-term">Collab Remix</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shorts remix format that places a creator's recording side-by-side with an eligible source Short, enabling duet-style reactions, responses, and continuations within a single published Short.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/collab-remix/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-collaborations/" class="glossary-card-term">Collaborations</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The broader practice of creators partnering on content across any format — co-hosted videos, guest appearances, joint live streams, or cross-promotional shoutouts. Pursued primarily to reach each other's audiences.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-collaborations/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/commerce-product-module/" class="glossary-card-term">Commerce Product Module</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's contract that enables eligible Partner Program creators to earn from fan-funding features — channel memberships, Super Chat, Super Stickers, and Super Thanks — for 70% of net revenue after applicable taxes and fees.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/commerce-product-module/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-communities/" class="glossary-card-term">Communities</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube feature (general availability June 2025) that gives subscribers a dedicated space to start discussions with each other and the creator, separate from comment sections and Community posts.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-communities/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-community-tab/" class="glossary-card-term">Community Tab</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The section of a YouTube channel (officially renamed "Posts" in 2025) where creators share text updates, polls, images, and video links between uploads to maintain audience engagement.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-community-tab/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/concurrent-viewers/" class="glossary-card-term">Concurrent Viewers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The number of people watching a YouTube live stream at the same moment. This real-time metric is visible in the Live Control Room and is the standard benchmark for measuring live stream reach.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/concurrent-viewers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-calendar/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Calendar</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An operational schedule that tracks what a creator plans to publish, when it goes live, and what production work must happen before and after publication. A planning tool for videos, Shorts, live streams, posts, and promotion — distinct from a general upload schedule, which only states posting frequency.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-calendar/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-creator/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Creator</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A person who produces and publishes original video content on YouTube for an audience. The term applies across all niches, channel sizes, and monetization levels — from hobby creators to full-time professionals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-creator/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-entrepreneur/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Entrepreneur</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator who builds a business around their content by diversifying income across multiple revenue streams — ads, sponsorships, memberships, digital products — rather than depending on a single platform payout.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-entrepreneur/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-gap/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Gap</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube search gap where viewers cannot find enough relevant, exact, current, or high-quality results for a query. Found through the Trends tab's Content Gaps for Shorts card, gaps signal a creation opportunity — not a guaranteed ranking or traffic outcome.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-gap/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-id/" class="glossary-card-term">Content ID</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's automated copyright system that scans uploads for audio or video matching a rights-holder's registered content. Matches can result in the video being claimed, monetized by the rights-holder, muted, or blocked entirely.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-id/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-pillar/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Pillar</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A recurring subject area or audience need that a creator intentionally covers across multiple videos and formats — a planning framework for keeping channel coverage coherent, not a YouTube Studio setting or algorithm factor. Three to five pillars is a common range, but no specific number is required.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-pillar/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-repurposing/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Repurposing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The process of adapting an existing video, recording, or asset into a new format, length, or distribution channel — such as turning a long tutorial into a Short, a livestream into focused clips, or a transcript into a written guide. Repurposing is adaptation, not simple reposting: each derivative should stand alone and serve the new audience's needs.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-repurposing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/copyright-checks/" class="glossary-card-term">Copyright Checks</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's upload-stage scan for potential Content ID matches before a video is published. Flags copyrighted content so creators can review and resolve claims — but results are not final and future manual claims remain possible.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/copyright-checks/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/copyright-claim/" class="glossary-card-term">Copyright Claim</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A Content ID notification indicating a video contains material owned by a third party. The rights-holder can choose to monetize the video, mute the flagged audio, or block the video in certain countries or globally.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/copyright-claim/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/copyright-strike/" class="glossary-card-term">Copyright Strike</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A formal legal takedown issued to a YouTube channel for using copyrighted content without permission. Three active strikes result in channel termination; even one strike restricts channel features for 90 days.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/copyright-strike/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-corrections/" class="glossary-card-term">Corrections</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube feature that lets creators add timestamped factual corrections to a published video's description. YouTube automatically surfaces an in-player info card to viewers — no re-upload or separate form required.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-corrections/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-create/" class="glossary-card-term">Create App</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's standalone mobile video editor (YouTube Create) designed for Shorts production, offering auto-captions, filters, transitions, and a music library in a simpler interface than desktop editing software.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-create/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creative-commons/" class="glossary-card-term">Creative Commons</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Standardized free copyright licenses that allow creators to legally use, remix, or share others' work under specified conditions. Creators can license their YouTube videos under Creative Commons to permit reuse by others.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creative-commons/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-agency/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Agency</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A company that represents multiple creators, handling brand deal negotiations, partnerships, management, and strategy on their behalf, typically in exchange for a percentage of the creator's earnings.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-agency/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-manager/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Manager</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An individual who handles the business side of a creator's career — negotiating deals, managing partnerships, advising on growth strategy, and connecting them with opportunities — typically for a percentage of earnings.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-manager/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-creator-partnerships/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Partnerships</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's official brand-deal tool (formerly BrandConnect) that connects eligible Partner Program creators with brands seeking sponsorships. Creators receive and manage campaign inquiries directly inside YouTube Studio.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-creator-partnerships/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-educator/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator-Educator</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator whose content is primarily educational, teaching skills, subjects, or practical knowledge. Often pursues monetization through courses, affiliate programs, and brand deals in addition to ad revenue.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-educator/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/custom-emoji/" class="glossary-card-term">Custom Emoji</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Channel-specific images that active channel members can use in comments and live chat, uploaded and named by the creator through YouTube Studio Memberships. All active members receive access to the full emoji library regardless of membership level — more slots unlock as the channel's member count grows.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/custom-emoji/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/custom-thumbnail/" class="glossary-card-term">Custom Thumbnail</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator-uploaded image that replaces YouTube's auto-generated video frame, appearing in Home, Search, Suggested, and other surfaces — the primary visual element viewers use to decide whether to click and watch.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/custom-thumbnail/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cut-remix/" class="glossary-card-term">Cut Remix</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shorts tool that samples a 1–5 second segment (video and audio) from an eligible YouTube video and lets creators build a new Short around it as a hook, reaction, or quick reference.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cut-remix/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-d">D</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-demographics/" class="glossary-card-term">Demographics</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Data about a channel's audience including age, gender, and geographic location. Creators use demographics to understand their viewers and to pitch advertisers on why their audience matches the brand's target customer.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-channel-demographics/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/device-type/" class="glossary-card-term">Device Type</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics report showing what percentage of a channel's watch time comes from mobile, computer, TV, and tablet — ordered from the highest to lowest share and filterable by content type.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/device-type/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/direct-or-unknown-traffic/" class="glossary-card-term">Direct or Unknown Traffic</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics traffic-source category for views from direct URL entry, bookmarks, signed-out viewers, and apps or sources that do not provide identifiable referral data. Not a sign of invalid traffic — many legitimate sharing paths strip referral information.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/direct-or-unknown-traffic/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/dream-screen/" class="glossary-card-term">Dream Screen</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube AI feature inside the Shorts camera that generates image or video backgrounds from a text prompt, usable as a green-screen backdrop or as a standalone clip inserted anywhere in a Short.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/dream-screen/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/dropped-frames/" class="glossary-card-term">Dropped Frames</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Frames a computer fails to render and transmit in time during a live stream, resulting in choppy or stuttering video for viewers. Typically caused by insufficient CPU/GPU performance or limited upload bandwidth.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/dropped-frames/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-e">E</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/editorial-calendar/" class="glossary-card-term">Editorial Calendar</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A high-level planning document that maps the themes, audience goals, campaigns, recurring programs, and seasonal priorities a YouTube channel intends to cover over time. Answers strategic questions before the creator commits to specific scripts — distinct from the content calendar, which tracks individual deliverables and production dates.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/editorial-calendar/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-embeds/" class="glossary-card-term">Embeds</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube videos placed and played on external websites using an embed code. Embedded views appear in a creator's analytics under the "Embedded player" traffic source and count toward total view metrics.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-embeds/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/end-screens/" class="glossary-card-term">End Screens</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Clickable overlay elements added to the final 5–20 seconds of a YouTube video prompting viewers to watch another video, subscribe, or visit an external link. A core tool for extending watch sessions within a creator's content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/end-screens/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/end-screens-traffic/" class="glossary-card-term">End Screens Traffic</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Views attributed to clicks on creator end-screen video or playlist elements during the final 5–20 seconds of a video. Separate from end-screen click rate, which measures how often elements were clicked on the source video.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/end-screens-traffic/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/engaged-views/" class="glossary-card-term">Engaged Views</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shorts metric counting viewers who watched past the first few seconds rather than immediately swiping away. YouTube uses engaged views — not total views — to determine monetization eligibility and YPP thresholds.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/engaged-views/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/estimated-revenue/" class="glossary-card-term">Estimated Revenue</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube Analytics' provisional calculation of a creator's earnings from ads, Premium, memberships, and Supers during a selected period. Subject to adjustment before finalization — not the same as the amount YouTube will pay.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/estimated-revenue/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/evergreen-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Evergreen Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube video designed to remain useful beyond a short news cycle or trend window by answering a recurring viewer need — how-to tutorials, definitions, and beginner guides are common examples. Evergreen is a creator-strategy term, not a YouTube setting, and most durable content still requires periodic review as products, policies, and platforms change.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/evergreen-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/external-traffic/" class="glossary-card-term">External Traffic</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube traffic from websites and apps outside YouTube — including Google Search, social platforms, news sites, blogs, and embedded players. Tracked separately from YouTube Search and shown in the External sites or app report in Analytics.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/external-traffic/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-f">F</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/faceless-channel/" class="glossary-card-term">Faceless Channel</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube channel where the creator never appears on camera, relying instead on voiceovers, animation, screen recordings, or stock footage. Common in finance, history, and tutorial niches where personal identity is less central.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/faceless-channel/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/fan-funding/" class="glossary-card-term">Fan Funding</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A broad category of viewer-supported revenue on YouTube — Super Chat, Super Stickers, Super Thanks, and channel memberships — all ways fans can directly pay creators as appreciation or ongoing support.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/fan-funding/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/featured-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Featured Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video selected in the channel Home tab's Spotlight area for returning subscribers — different from the channel trailer, which targets non-subscribers. YouTube stops showing it to a viewer after they watch it, making it a rotating priority rather than a permanent placement.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/featured-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/finalized-earnings/" class="glossary-card-term">Finalized Earnings</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The previous month's YouTube earnings after Google's monthly finalization process, posted to AdSense for YouTube between the 7th and 12th of the following month. Not the same as payment, which is issued later when thresholds and verification are met.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/finalized-earnings/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/formats-your-viewers-watch/" class="glossary-card-term">Formats Your Viewers Watch</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics report showing which content types — videos, Shorts, and live streams — your viewers watch across YouTube in the past 28 days, helping creators evaluate format experiments before committing to them.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/formats-your-viewers-watch/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-g">G</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/gift-membership/" class="glossary-card-term">Gift Membership</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A one-month channel membership purchased by a creator or viewer and distributed by YouTube to eligible opted-in subscribers during a live stream or Premiere. Non-recurring and cannot be directed to a specific recipient.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/gift-membership/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-gifts/" class="glossary-card-term">Gifts</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Animated virtual items YouTube viewers send during eligible live streams by spending Jewels (YouTube's virtual currency). Creators earn Rubies for each Gift received, representing direct fan-to-creator payment during live streams.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-gifts/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/green-screen-remix/" class="glossary-card-term">Green Screen Remix</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shorts remix format that places source video as a full-screen background behind a creator who records in front of it, enabling commentary or reaction videos with the original content always visible.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/green-screen-remix/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-h">H</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-handles/" class="glossary-card-term">Handles</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Unique @usernames on YouTube (e.g., @CreatorName) that give every channel a consistent, searchable identity across the platform. Handles appear in search results, video descriptions, and can tag creators in comments.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-handles/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/hashtags/" class="glossary-card-term">Hashtags</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Words preceded by # added to video titles or descriptions that help YouTube categorize content and surface it in hashtag search results. Most effective when used sparingly with highly relevant terms.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/hashtags/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/heart-a-comment/" class="glossary-card-term">Heart a Comment</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator-only action that places the channel's avatar with a red heart on a viewer's comment to show appreciation. Depending on the viewer's notification settings YouTube may alert them — and a separate AI tool in the Studio mobile app suggests recent comments worth hearting.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/heart-a-comment/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/hidden-user/" class="glossary-card-term">Hidden User</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A channel-wide YouTube moderation action that silently prevents a viewer's comments, live chat messages, Community posts, and clip creation from being visible across a creator's channel. The viewer is not notified, previous comments are hidden within 48 hours, and hidden comments cannot be reviewed in the Held queue.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/hidden-user/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-hype/" class="glossary-card-term">Hype</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube discovery feature for channels with 500–500,000 subscribers where viewers give free "hype points" to recent videos, boosting them on a weekly country-specific leaderboard to help smaller creators gain visibility.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-hype/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-i">I</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-impressions/" class="glossary-card-term">Impressions</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The number of times YouTube shows a video's thumbnail to signed-in viewers. Impressions are the top of the click-through funnel and are tracked in YouTube Studio's Reach tab alongside click-through rate.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-impressions/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/influencer-agency/" class="glossary-card-term">Influencer Agency</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A company that manages relationships between brands and creators, facilitating sponsorship deals, handling contracts, and taking a commission — similar to a talent agency but focused on digital content partnerships.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/influencer-agency/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/influencers/" class="glossary-card-term">Influencers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Creators with established audiences who can shape followers' opinions and purchasing decisions. The term is commonly used in brand partnership contexts and covers creators across YouTube, Instagram, TikTok, and other platforms.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/influencers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-inspiration-tab/" class="glossary-card-term">Inspiration Tab</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Studio feature powered by AI that suggests video ideas based on trending topics, a creator's audience interests, and gaps in their existing content catalog. Helps creators identify what to make next.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-inspiration-tab/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/intro-retention/" class="glossary-card-term">Intro Retention</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The percentage of viewers still watching after the first 30 seconds of a video — used to evaluate whether the opening delivered on the title and thumbnail promise and whether it outperforms the channel's typical intros.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/intro-retention/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-j">J</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-jewels/" class="glossary-card-term">Jewels</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's virtual currency that viewers purchase in the mobile app and spend to send animated Gifts to creators during live streams. When a Gift is sent, the creator earns Rubies — YouTube's unit for gift-based earnings.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-jewels/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-k">K</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/key-moments-for-audience-retention/" class="glossary-card-term">Key Moments for Audience Retention</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics report that identifies notable points in a video's retention curve — including the intro percentage, top moments, spikes, and dips — to help creators understand where viewer attention changed.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/key-moments-for-audience-retention/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/keywords/" class="glossary-card-term">Keywords</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Specific words and phrases added to a video's title, description, and tags to help YouTube and Google understand the content and match it to relevant viewer searches. Keyword research is a foundation of YouTube SEO.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/keywords/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-l">L</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-likeness-detection/" class="glossary-card-term">Likeness Detection</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An experimental YouTube Studio feature that scans newly uploaded videos for AI-generated or AI-altered content featuring an enrolled creator's face, alerting them to potential deepfakes and routing them to a removal request process.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-likeness-detection/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-live/" class="glossary-card-term">Live</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's feature for broadcasting real-time video to an audience via the mobile app, YouTube Studio, or third-party software. Supports live chat, fan funding tools, and concurrent viewer metrics during the broadcast.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-live/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/live-chat-replay/" class="glossary-card-term">Live Chat Replay</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The archived chat experience that plays messages alongside a completed live stream at the times they originally appeared. On by default for eligible archives — but any YouTube Video Editor change (trimming, blurring, cutting) permanently removes the replay.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/live-chat-replay/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/live-control-room/" class="glossary-card-term">Live Control Room</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The YouTube Studio dashboard used to manage an active live stream, showing real-time viewer counts, chat moderation tools, stream health metrics, and broadcast settings all in one place.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/live-control-room/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/live-dvr/" class="glossary-card-term">Live DVR</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube feature that lets viewers rewind, pause, and replay an in-progress live stream up to a set buffer limit, allowing late arrivals to catch up without waiting for the stream to end.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/live-dvr/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/live-encoder/" class="glossary-card-term">Live Encoder</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Third-party software or hardware (like OBS Studio or Streamlabs) that captures, encodes, and transmits a video signal to YouTube's servers via an RTMP connection during a live stream.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/live-encoder/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/live-redirect/" class="glossary-card-term">Live Redirect</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube feature that sends viewers watching one live stream directly to another channel's live stream at the end of a broadcast. Used for handoffs, co-streams, and directing audiences to partner creators.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/live-redirect/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/low-latency/" class="glossary-card-term">Low Latency</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube live stream setting that reduces the delay between broadcast and what viewers see to roughly 2–7 seconds. Recommended when creator-viewer interaction like live Q&A is more important than maximum video quality.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/low-latency/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/loyalty-badge/" class="glossary-card-term">Loyalty Badge</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A small channel-membership icon shown beside an active member's name in comments, live chat, and channel posts, representing accumulated active paid membership time — not calendar time. Milestones range from new member to five years; creators can use default or custom badge designs for each slot.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/loyalty-badge/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-m">M</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/made-for-kids/" class="glossary-card-term">Made for Kids (MFK)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video designation that triggers COPPA compliance rules on YouTube, disabling personalized ads, comments, end screens, cards, and most monetization features. Creators must accurately label their intended audience in Studio.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/made-for-kids/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/members-only-chat/" class="glossary-card-term">Members-Only Chat</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube live-chat setting that restricts message posting to active channel members while the stream itself remains publicly viewable — giving members participation rights in chat without hiding the broadcast behind a paywall.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/members-only-chat/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/members-only-live-stream/" class="glossary-card-term">Members-Only Live Stream</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube live broadcast restricted to active channel members at the selected tier — either started as members-only from the beginning or transitioned from a public stream using YouTube's countdown workflow, which creates two separate stream records sharing one stream key.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/members-only-live-stream/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/members-only-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Members-Only Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube upload whose playback is restricted to qualifying channel members at a selected tier, though non-members can still discover the title and thumbnail. Higher membership levels automatically inherit access to lower-level exclusive videos.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/members-only-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/membership-perks/" class="glossary-card-term">Membership Perks</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The exclusive benefits a YouTube creator offers recurring channel members — including badges, emoji, early access, members-only content, live streams, and chat access — organized across up to six tiers of one to five perks each, with higher tiers automatically inheriting lower-tier benefits.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/membership-perks/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/monetized-playbacks/" class="glossary-card-term">Monetized Playbacks</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The count of video views where at least one ad was actually served to the viewer. Not every view includes an ad, so monetized playbacks — not total views — are the accurate basis for calculating ad earnings.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/monetized-playbacks/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/monthly-audience/" class="glossary-card-term">Monthly Audience</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's rolling estimate of the distinct viewers who watched a channel in the previous 28 days, recalculated every day and broken into new, casual, and regular viewer segments to show active audience size.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/monthly-audience/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/multi-channel-network/" class="glossary-card-term">Multi-Channel Network (MCN)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A company that partners with multiple YouTube creators to offer services like production support, brand deal access, and audience development, typically in exchange for a share of the creators' ad revenue.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/multi-channel-network/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/multi-language-audio/" class="glossary-card-term">Multi-Language Audio</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube feature that lets creators upload separate audio tracks in different languages for the same video, giving international viewers the option to watch in their preferred language without a separate video upload.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/multi-language-audio/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-n">N</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/new-viewers/" class="glossary-card-term">New Viewers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics audience segment for people who watched a channel for the first time in a given period — including viewers using private browsing or who have not watched in over a year.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/new-viewers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/niche/" class="glossary-card-term">Niche</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The specific topic, audience, or content category a creator focuses on. A well-defined niche helps the algorithm understand who to recommend the channel to and gives creators a clearer positioning advantage in their corner of YouTube.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/niche/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/normal-latency/" class="glossary-card-term">Normal Latency</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The default YouTube live stream latency setting, delivering the best video quality with a 15–30+ second delay between broadcast and viewer. Better for quality-focused streams where real-time chat interaction is less critical.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/normal-latency/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/notifications-traffic/" class="glossary-card-term">Notifications Traffic</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube Analytics traffic from notifications and emails sent to a channel's subscribers, covering belled notifications (All notifications) and other app and email notifications. Not the same as the Subscriptions feed, which is part of Browse Features.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/notifications-traffic/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-o">O</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/open-loop/" class="glossary-card-term">Open Loop</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A storytelling device where a creator introduces an unanswered question or unresolved promise to hold viewer attention, then closes it by delivering the answer or payoff. An open loop is creator-strategy vocabulary — not an official YouTube feature or metric.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/open-loop/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-outro/" class="glossary-card-term">Outro</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The closing portion of a YouTube video that resolves the main promise, delivers a final takeaway, and directs viewers toward a next action such as a recommended video or subscribe prompt. Different from an end screen, which is an interactive overlay added through YouTube Studio.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-outro/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-p">P</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/peak-concurrent-viewers/" class="glossary-card-term">Peak Concurrent Viewers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The highest number of people watching a live stream simultaneously at any single moment during the broadcast. A key benchmark for measuring a live stream's total reach and audience engagement.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/peak-concurrent-viewers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/personal-brand/" class="glossary-card-term">Personal Brand</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The public identity a creator builds — their voice, aesthetic, values, and perceived expertise — that makes them recognizable and distinct from others making similar content. The foundation of long-term creator audience loyalty.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/personal-brand/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/pinned-comment/" class="glossary-card-term">Pinned Comment</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A comment a YouTube creator places at the top of a video's or post's comment section so viewers see it first — whether it's the creator's own comment or a viewer's. Only one comment can be pinned at a time, the feature requires Advanced feature access, and only the channel owner (not comment moderators) can pin.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/pinned-comment/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/playback-based-cpm/" class="glossary-card-term">Playback-Based CPM</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The amount advertisers pay per 1,000 monetized playbacks on a creator's content. Different from YouTube's raw CPM, playback-based CPM is what creators can actually track in YouTube Studio and most directly reflects their ad earnings rate.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/playback-based-cpm/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-playlists/" class="glossary-card-term">Playlist</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A curated collection of YouTube videos grouped together by a creator or viewer. Playlists appear as a traffic source when viewers watch multiple videos in sequence and can significantly boost a channel's total watch time.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-playlists/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/playlist-traffic/" class="glossary-card-term">Playlist Traffic</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube Analytics traffic from any playlist containing your video, including your own, another creator's, and viewers' Liked Videos and Favorites playlists. Indicates a view came through a playlist context, not necessarily sequential autoplay.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/playlist-traffic/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-podcasts/" class="glossary-card-term">Podcasts</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube content format for audio-first or long-form conversation-style video, often with a dedicated podcast tab on the channel. YouTube has invested heavily in hosting and promoting podcast content as a distinct format.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-podcasts/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-premieres/" class="glossary-card-term">Premieres</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube feature that schedules a video to go live at a specific future time, with a countdown and shared live chat. Lets creators build anticipation and watch simultaneously with their audience as a community event.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-premieres/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/private-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Private Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube upload viewable only by the creator and specifically invited accounts. Private videos don't appear in search or subscriber feeds, have no comments, and can't be publicly embedded — but YouTube can still review them for copyright and policy.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/private-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/production-company/" class="glossary-card-term">Production Company</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A business that creates video content on behalf of brands or other clients, handling scripting, filming, editing, and delivery. Some creators structure their own channel operations as formal production companies.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/production-company/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/profile-picture/" class="glossary-card-term">Profile Picture</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The circular image displayed on a YouTube channel and in comments. A creator's most visible brand identifier on the platform — should be a clear, recognizable image that remains legible even at small display sizes.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/profile-picture/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/public-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Public Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube upload that anyone on the platform can watch. Public status makes a video eligible for search, recommendations, subscriber feeds, and embeds — but doesn't guarantee reach, notifications to every subscriber, or freedom from copyright or age restrictions.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/public-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/publishing-cadence/" class="glossary-card-term">Publishing Cadence</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The recurring frequency and rhythm with which a creator releases content — such as weekly long-form videos, two Shorts per week, or a monthly live stream. Distinct from an upload schedule (which maps actual dates) and from consistency (the ability to meet recognizable standards and expectations over time).</p>
  <a href="/glossary/publishing-cadence/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-r">R</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/recommended-videos/" class="glossary-card-term">Recommended Videos</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The videos YouTube surfaces in the suggested panel alongside whatever a viewer is currently watching. Appearing here is a major views driver and is influenced by a video's relevance to the viewer's watch history.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/recommended-videos/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/regular-viewers/" class="glossary-card-term">Regular Viewers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics metric measuring viewers who have watched a channel's content on at least 3 different days in the past 28 days. Represents the channel's most loyal and consistently returning segment of the audience.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/regular-viewers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-remix/" class="glossary-card-term">Remix</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's suite of built-in tools (Cut, Collab, Green Screen, Sound) that let creators legally sample portions of other creators' videos or audio when making Shorts. Source creators receive attribution and control remix availability.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-remix/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/retention/" class="glossary-card-term">Retention</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">How long viewers watch a video before leaving, tracked as average view duration and a retention curve. Higher retention signals viewer satisfaction and directly influences how aggressively YouTube recommends the video to others.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/retention/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/retention-dips/" class="glossary-card-term">Retention Dips</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Downward movements in a YouTube retention graph where viewers watched a section less than surrounding parts — caused by skipping, exits, chapter navigation, answer completion, or expectation mismatches between the title and the content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/retention-dips/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/retention-spikes/" class="glossary-card-term">Retention Spikes</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Upward movements in a YouTube retention graph where a section received more viewing activity than surrounding parts — indicating rewatching, sharing, direct seeking, or confusion that caused viewers to replay the moment.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/retention-spikes/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/returning-viewers/" class="glossary-card-term">Returning Viewers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Viewers who have previously watched a channel and come back for more in a given period. A key audience health indicator showing that content is building habitual viewership rather than just attracting one-off visitors.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/returning-viewers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/reused-content/" class="glossary-card-term">Reused Content</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Content uploaded to YouTube in the same or very similar form as content elsewhere, with little or no original transformation, commentary, or creative addition. Heavy reliance on reused content can disqualify a channel from monetization.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/reused-content/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/royalty-free-music/" class="glossary-card-term">Royalty-Free Music</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Music licensed for use in YouTube videos without paying ongoing royalties per use. Available through third-party platforms and YouTube's own Audio Library, though "royalty-free" doesn't always mean free to use commercially without a license.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/royalty-free-music/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-rpm/" class="glossary-card-term">RPM (Revenue Per Mille)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Studio metric showing how much a creator earns per 1,000 total video views, blending all revenue sources — ads, memberships, Super Chat, and Premium. A useful overall earnings benchmark, but not the same as CPM.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-rpm/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/rtmp/" class="glossary-card-term">RTMP</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The streaming protocol (Real-Time Messaging Protocol) used to send a live video signal from third-party encoder software like OBS to YouTube's servers. Creators connect via a stream key and RTMP server URL in their encoder settings.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/rtmp/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-s">S</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/scheduled-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Scheduled Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube upload set to become Public automatically at a chosen date, time, and time zone. The video stays Private before publication, letting creators complete processing and checks before the video reaches the subscriber feed.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/scheduled-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/search-query/" class="glossary-card-term">Search Query</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The exact wording a viewer types into YouTube Search, expressing what they are trying to find at that moment. Distinct from keywords (a creator's target phrase) and from the Search Terms report, which shows only queries that actually drove traffic to the channel.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/search-query/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/searches-across-youtube/" class="glossary-card-term">Searches Across YouTube</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An older label for the Searched on YouTube card in YouTube Studio's Trends tab, showing top search queries based on the creator's audience and saved searches over the last 28 days — not a complete database of all YouTube searches.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/searches-across-youtube/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/seo/" class="glossary-card-term">SEO</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The practice of crafting titles, descriptions, tags, and content around words viewers actually search for, to improve a video's visibility in YouTube and Google search results. The primary free long-term channel growth lever.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/seo/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/series-playlist/" class="glossary-card-term">Series Playlist</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An official YouTube playlist designation marking a creator-owned set of videos intended to be viewed together. Requires a verified account, limits each video to one official series, and may allow YouTube to modify how those videos are presented or discovered.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/series-playlist/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shadow-banning/" class="glossary-card-term">Shadow Banning</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An informal term for when a creator believes their content is being suppressed in recommendations or search without notification. YouTube doesn't officially acknowledge shadow banning; reduced reach more commonly reflects algorithm performance signals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shadow-banning/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-shorts/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's vertical, short-form video format for videos under 3 minutes. Shorts appear in a dedicated swipeable feed and are YouTube's direct competitor to TikTok and Instagram Reels, built for quick mobile viewing.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-shorts/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-draft/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Draft</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An unfinished Short saved inside the YouTube mobile app for later editing or upload. Stored on the device, not the YouTube channel — deleting the app or replacing the phone permanently removes all drafts, with no cloud sync or account restore provided.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-draft/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-engaged-views/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Engaged Views</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics count of viewers who stayed to watch a Short past its initial seconds, excluding loops. YouTube uses engaged views — not the broader post-2025 public view count — for audience retention calculations, YPP eligibility, and Shorts revenue sharing.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-engaged-views/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-feed/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Feed</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's continuous vertical viewing experience for discovering and watching short-form videos. Viewers swipe through items one at a time in the vertical player — separate from the Shorts shelf, the Shorts tab, and regular watch pages.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-feed/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-feed-ads/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Feed Ads</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Ads shown between Shorts as viewers scroll the YouTube Shorts Feed. Revenue pools monthly, is split between music licensing and a Creator Pool, and eligible creators keep 45% of their allocation based on engaged-view share.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-feed-ads/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-feed-traffic/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Feed Traffic</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics traffic source counting views attributed to the vertical Shorts viewing experience — not the same as Shown in Feed (exposure count) or total Shorts views (which can come from Search, Channel Pages, and other sources).</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-feed-traffic/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-monetization-module/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Monetization Module</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's contract enabling eligible Partner Program creators to share pooled Shorts Feed ad revenue and Premium revenue from eligible Shorts. Sharing begins on the acceptance date; earlier views are not retroactively eligible.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-monetization-module/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-remixing/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Remixing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's set of in-product tools for building a new Short from eligible audio, video, templates, or AI transformations connected to existing content — including Sound, Cut, Green Screen, Collab, and Template options. Remixing through the official tools preserves source attribution and applies platform permissions.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-remixing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-thumbnail/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Thumbnail</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The preview image representing a Short on surfaces like Search, channel pages, and hashtag pages — selected from a video frame via the YouTube mobile app, not uploaded as a separate custom image. The selected frame matters most outside the Shorts Feed, where the opening playback frame determines first impressions.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-thumbnail/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shorts-views/" class="glossary-card-term">Shorts Views</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's public count of legitimate Shorts play starts and replays, measured without a minimum watch-time requirement since March 31, 2025. Distinct from Engaged Views, which still require viewing past the initial seconds and are used for YPP eligibility and monetization calculations.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shorts-views/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/slow-mode/" class="glossary-card-term">Slow Mode</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube live-chat setting that requires ordinary participants to wait for a creator-selected period between messages, reducing message frequency without restricting who can participate. Channel owners, moderators, and active paid members are exempt from the delay.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/slow-mode/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sound-remix/" class="glossary-card-term">Sound Remix</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shorts remix tool that samples only the audio — music, dialogue, or sound effects — from an eligible YouTube video, letting creators build new Shorts around a trending sound without using the source visuals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sound-remix/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/stayed-to-watch/" class="glossary-card-term">Stayed to Watch</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shorts analytics metric showing the percentage of viewers who kept watching past a Short's opening seconds instead of swiping away. Essentially the hook success rate — the first signal YouTube uses to decide whether to distribute a Short more broadly.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/stayed-to-watch/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/stream-bitrate/" class="glossary-card-term">Stream Bitrate</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The amount of data per second a live encoder sends to YouTube during a broadcast. Higher bitrates produce better video quality but require more upload bandwidth. YouTube recommends specific bitrates depending on resolution and frame rate.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/stream-bitrate/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/stream-key/" class="glossary-card-term">Stream Key</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A unique private code that connects a third-party encoder like OBS to a creator's specific YouTube channel, authorizing it to send a live video signal. Should be kept secret — anyone with it can stream to the channel.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/stream-key/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/stream-latency/" class="glossary-card-term">Stream Latency</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The delay between what a creator broadcasts and what viewers see during a live stream. YouTube offers ultra-low, low, and normal settings — lower latency enables better real-time interaction but sacrifices some video quality.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/stream-latency/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sub-for-sub/" class="glossary-card-term">Sub for Sub</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A practice where creators subscribe to each other purely to inflate counts, with no genuine interest in the content. The algorithm ignores these hollow subscribers because they never engage, making Sub for Sub useless for actual growth.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sub-for-sub/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/subscriber-only-chat/" class="glossary-card-term">Subscriber-Only Chat</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube live-chat setting that restricts message posting to subscribed viewers, optionally requiring a minimum subscription time before they can participate. Subscriptions are free — this is not a paid feature — and it cannot run simultaneously with members-only chat.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/subscriber-only-chat/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-subscribers/" class="glossary-card-term">Subscribers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Viewers who have clicked Subscribe on a YouTube channel to receive notifications about new uploads. Subscriber count is a visible metric, but engagement quality and watch habits matter far more to algorithmic reach than raw subscriber numbers.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-subscribers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/suggested-videos/" class="glossary-card-term">Suggested Videos</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Videos YouTube surfaces in the "Up Next" panel alongside whatever a viewer is currently watching. Appearing here is a high-value traffic source algorithmically matched to viewer taste, often responsible for the majority of a video's long-term views.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/suggested-videos/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/super-chat/" class="glossary-card-term">Super Chat</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A paid feature on YouTube live streams where viewers pay to have their comment pinned and highlighted in chat for a set period, making it more visible to the creator and everyone watching.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/super-chat/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/super-stickers/" class="glossary-card-term">Super Stickers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Paid animated stickers viewers can send in a YouTube live chat to support a creator. They appear as visual overlays in the chat stream and represent a lighter-touch fan funding option compared to Super Chat.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/super-stickers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/super-thanks/" class="glossary-card-term">Super Thanks</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A paid feature that lets viewers leave a highlighted, colorful comment on a regular YouTube video — not just live streams — as a one-time tip to show appreciation for a specific piece of content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/super-thanks/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-supers/" class="glossary-card-term">Supers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's collective term for the three fan-funding features available to Partner Program creators: Super Chat, Super Stickers, and Super Thanks. Together they represent the platform's real-time and post-production tipping tools.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-supers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/swiped-away/" class="glossary-card-term">Swiped Away</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The outcome in YouTube's How many chose to view report where a Shorts Feed viewer moves past a Short before staying past the initial seconds. A fast swipe can still count as a public Shorts view since March 2025, but the playback does not qualify as an Engaged View.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/swiped-away/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-t">T</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/talent-manager/" class="glossary-card-term">Talent Manager</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A professional who manages the business side of a creator's career — negotiating deals, booking opportunities, advising on strategy, and connecting them with brands — typically for a percentage of the creator's earnings.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/talent-manager/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/test-and-compare/" class="glossary-card-term">Test and Compare</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The earlier name for YouTube's native thumbnail-testing feature, now expanded and rebranded as YouTube A/B Testing to include title-only, thumbnail-only, and combined title-and-thumbnail experiments selected by watch-time share.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/test-and-compare/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/thumbnail-and-title-test/" class="glossary-card-term">Thumbnail and Title Test</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube A/B experiment that compares up to three complete title-and-thumbnail packages for the same video, evaluating which full concept produces the strongest watch-time share without isolating one element.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/thumbnail-and-title-test/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/thumbnail-packaging/" class="glossary-card-term">Thumbnail Packaging</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator-strategy term for how a video's thumbnail visually presents the subject, composition, contrast, and visual promise — working alongside the title to attract the right viewers before they click.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/thumbnail-packaging/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/thumbnail-test/" class="glossary-card-term">Thumbnail Test</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube A/B experiment that compares up to three custom thumbnails for the same video while keeping the title constant, selected by watch-time share to identify which image drives stronger viewing — not just more clicks.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/thumbnail-test/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-thumbnails/" class="glossary-card-term">Thumbnails</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The preview images displayed for YouTube videos in search results, feeds, and suggested panels. Thumbnails are the single most important visual factor in whether a viewer clicks on a video — outweighing almost everything else.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-thumbnails/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/title-test/" class="glossary-card-term">Title Test</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube A/B experiment that compares up to three video titles while holding the thumbnail constant, helping creators compare wording strategies and identify which drives stronger watch-time share.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/title-test/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/topical-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Topical Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube video built around a current event, seasonal moment, product release, or cultural conversation where timing often affects how much opportunity exists. Topical is a creator-strategy label — not a YouTube visibility setting — and is distinct from trending (rapidly growing attention) and evergreen (durable recurring demand).</p>
  <a href="/glossary/topical-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/traffic-sources/" class="glossary-card-term">Traffic Sources</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube Analytics categories showing where views came from — browse features, search, suggested videos, external sites, direct links, and more. Understanding traffic sources helps creators identify which growth levers are actually working.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/traffic-sources/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/trending-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Trending Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video experiencing unusually strong or rapidly growing attention — either within a niche or on YouTube's category-specific public Trending Charts, which show the same ranked videos to all viewers in a given country, update roughly every 30 minutes, and exclude ad-purchased views from placement decisions.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/trending-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/typical-retention/" class="glossary-card-term">Typical Retention</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The gray comparison range YouTube displays behind an audience-retention curve, showing how the selected video performs against the creator's latest 10 similar-length videos at each point in the timeline.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/typical-retention/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-u">U</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ugc-creator/" class="glossary-card-term">UGC Creator</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator who produces video content specifically for brands to use in their advertising, rather than publishing on their own channel. UGC (User-Generated Content) creators are paid for the content itself, not for their personal audience size.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ugc-creator/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ultra-low-latency/" class="glossary-card-term">Ultra-Low Latency</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The fastest YouTube live stream latency setting, reducing the delay to roughly 1–2 seconds. Ideal for highly interactive streams where creators need to read and respond to chat comments as close to real-time as possible.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ultra-low-latency/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/unique-viewers/" class="glossary-card-term">Unique Viewers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics metric counting individual people who watched a channel's content in a given period, regardless of how many times they watched. Gives a more accurate picture of actual audience size than raw total view counts.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/unique-viewers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/unlisted-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Unlisted Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube video that doesn't appear on the channel or in search results but can be watched by anyone with the link. Not a secure access-control system — anyone can reshare the link, and adding it to a public playlist can make it searchable.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/unlisted-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/upload-schedule/" class="glossary-card-term">Upload Schedule</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator's plan for when videos, Shorts, live streams, and posts are expected to publish, including recurring release days, seasonal windows, planned breaks, and production buffers. Distinct from the YouTube Schedule button (which queues one video) and from publishing cadence, which describes only the frequency pattern.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/upload-schedule/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-v">V</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/vertical-live/" class="glossary-card-term">Vertical Live</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube live stream format in 9:16 portrait orientation designed for full-screen mobile viewing, discoverable in the Shorts feed. Can be combined with a standard horizontal stream to serve both mobile and desktop audiences at once.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/vertical-live/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-video-chapters/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Chapters</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Timestamp markers added to a video's description that create a clickable chapter navigation bar in the YouTube player. Chapters improve viewer experience on long videos, aid SEO, and let viewers jump directly to the section they need.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-video-chapters/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-video-description/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Description</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The text field beneath a YouTube video containing context, keywords, links, timestamps, and calls to action. A well-optimized description helps YouTube understand and rank the video and gives viewers and search engines more to work with.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-video-description/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-hooks/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Hooks</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The opening moments (typically the first 15–30 seconds) of a YouTube video designed to immediately capture attention and give viewers a compelling reason to keep watching. A strong hook is the most important factor in improving audience retention.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-hooks/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-packaging/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Packaging</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">How a YouTube video is presented to viewers before they watch, primarily through its title and thumbnail. The strategic combination that communicates the video's value, topic, and expected payoff so viewers decide whether to click.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-packaging/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-series/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Series</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A group of YouTube videos connected by a recurring concept, format, host, or ordered learning path — either informal branding or organized through an official YouTube series playlist. An official series playlist requires a verified channel and allows one video in only one such playlist at a time.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-series/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-video-tags/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Tags</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Keywords added in YouTube Studio when uploading a video to help YouTube categorize the content. Less impactful than titles and descriptions for SEO but useful for disambiguation and helping YouTube understand commonly misspelled topic names.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-video-tags/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-video-titles/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Titles</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The main text headline for a YouTube video displayed in search results, feeds, and on the watch page. Titles significantly influence click-through rate and should balance curiosity-driving language with relevant keywords viewers actually search for.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-video-titles/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-visibility/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Visibility</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The YouTube setting that controls who can watch a video and where it appears — Public, Unlisted, Private, or Scheduled. Visibility affects discoverability, sharing, and comments but does not override copyright, age, or Community Guidelines restrictions.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-visibility/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/viewed-vs-swiped-away/" class="glossary-card-term">Viewed vs. Swiped Away</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shorts Analytics comparison showing the percentage of feed presentations where viewers stayed past the opening seconds versus swiped away, displayed as How many chose to view. Not the same as impressions CTR — the feed is a vertical auto-playing experience, not a thumbnail click funnel.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/viewed-vs-swiped-away/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/viewer-satisfaction/" class="glossary-card-term">Viewer Satisfaction</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's broad assessment of whether viewers enjoyed a video, evaluated through surveys, likes, dislikes, feedback, and return behavior. There is no single creator-facing satisfaction score — creators must infer it from a combination of Analytics signals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/viewer-satisfaction/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/viral/" class="glossary-card-term">Viral</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Describes a video that spreads rapidly and widely beyond a creator's existing audience, typically through social sharing and algorithmic amplification. Going viral is unpredictable — usually driven by strong emotional responses or timely cultural relevance.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/viral/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/visual-remixes/" class="glossary-card-term">Visual Remixes</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Shorts that use eligible video imagery from another Short or YouTube video through Cut, Green Screen, Collab, or supported AI transformations — distinct from audio-only remixes. YouTube tracks traffic driven back to the original content through the Remixed Video traffic source.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/visual-remixes/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/vlog/" class="glossary-card-term">Vlog</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video diary or documentary-style YouTube format where creators share their daily life, experiences, or behind-the-scenes moments. Vlogs build personal connection with audiences and are one of the oldest and most durable YouTube content formats.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/vlog/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-w">W</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/watch-page-ads/" class="glossary-card-term">Watch Page Ads</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Ads shown before, during, after, or around eligible long-form and live YouTube videos. Creators who accept the Watch Page Monetization Module and turn on ads receive 55% of net qualifying revenue — but ads are never guaranteed on every view.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/watch-page-ads/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/watch-page-monetization-module/" class="glossary-card-term">Watch Page Monetization Module</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's contract enabling eligible Partner Program creators to earn ad and Premium revenue from public long-form and live videos — and supported embedded players. Requires separately turning on monetization for each eligible video.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/watch-page-monetization-module/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-watch-time/" class="glossary-card-term">Watch Time</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The total minutes viewers have spent watching a creator's videos. Watch time is one of YouTube's primary signals for determining how widely to recommend a video or channel in search and on the homepage.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-watch-time/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/watch-time-from-subscribers/" class="glossary-card-term">Watch Time from Subscribers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics report showing what percentage of a channel's watch time came from subscribed versus non-subscribed viewers — a watch-time share measure, not a viewer count, that helps creators gauge discovery and audience loyalty.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/watch-time-from-subscribers/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/what-your-audience-watches/" class="glossary-card-term">What Your Audience Watches</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics report showing videos, Shorts, live streams, and podcasts your viewers watched outside your channel in the past seven days — used to identify topic patterns, packaging ideas, and collaboration opportunities.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/what-your-audience-watches/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/when-your-viewers-are-on-youtube/" class="glossary-card-term">When Your Viewers Are on YouTube</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Analytics heatmap showing when the channel's viewers are active on YouTube across the last 28 days — recommended for scheduling Premieres, live streams, and community posts when real-time audience presence matters.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/when-your-viewers-are-on-youtube/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter" id="letter-y">Y</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-a-b-testing/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube A/B Testing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A native YouTube Studio feature that lets eligible creators test up to three titles, thumbnails, or combinations on one video concurrently, selecting a winner based on watch-time share rather than click-through rate.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-a-b-testing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-ads/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Ads</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The advertising formats brands buy to reach YouTube viewers, and the ad-supported model creators monetize through. Includes pre-roll, mid-roll, bumper, and Shorts ads — all generating ad revenue that flows to eligible Partner Program creators.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-ads/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-blur-tool/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Blur Tool</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Studio Editor feature that obscures faces or selected areas of an already uploaded video using face detection or custom drawn boxes with fixed or tracked positioning. Saved blurs are irreversible through Studio as of June 2025.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-blur-tool/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-checks/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Checks</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The upload-stage screening process in YouTube Studio that reviews copyright issues and, for eligible Partner Program creators, advertiser suitability before publication. Results are not final and creators can publish while checks continue.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-checks/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-cpm/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube CPM (cost per mille)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The gross rate advertisers pay per 1,000 ad impressions before YouTube takes its 45% cut. Not what creators actually receive — that's playback-based CPM or RPM. CPMs vary widely by niche, geography, and season.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-cpm/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-editor/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Editor</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The browser-based video editor inside YouTube Studio for making limited post-upload changes — trimming, blurring, adding Audio Library music, and adjusting end screens — without re-uploading. Saved changes are not revertible through Revert to original as of June 2025.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-editor/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-partner-program/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Partner Program (YPP)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">YouTube's monetization program giving eligible creators access to ad revenue sharing, fan funding, Shopping, and creator support. Requires 1,000 subscribers and 4,000 watch hours (or 10 million Shorts views in 90 days) to unlock ad revenue.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-partner-program/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-payment-threshold/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Payment Threshold</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The minimum finalized balance a creator's AdSense for YouTube payments account must reach before Google issues a regular payment. For U.S.-dollar accounts the threshold is $100; the balance rolls forward month to month rather than being forfeited.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-payment-threshold/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-poll/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Poll</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An interactive question creators can add to posts, live chat, Shorts, or members-only content — available as text, image, or live-chat polls, each with different creation rules and up to four answer options for the post format.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-poll/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-premium-revenue/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Premium Revenue</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Revenue YouTube pays eligible creators when YouTube Premium members watch their content. Funded by subscription fees rather than ads, distributed based on viewing, and separate from ad revenue — requiring the applicable YPP monetization module.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-premium-revenue/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-search-terms/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Search Terms</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The popular queries viewers used before finding a creator's content through YouTube Search, shown in the Analytics Search Terms report. A filtered subset of traffic, not a complete database of all searches related to the topic.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-search-terms/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-self-certification/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Self-Certification</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A monetization feature for eligible YouTube Partner Program creators that asks them to rate their own videos against advertiser-friendly guidelines before enabling ads. Accuracy history influences how much YouTube relies on the creator's input for the initial monetization decision.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-self-certification/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-shopping/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Shopping</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube feature that lets eligible creators tag products in their videos, Shorts, and live streams — from their own store or affiliate partners — so viewers can browse and purchase without leaving YouTube.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-shopping/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-studio/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Studio</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The creator dashboard where all channel management happens — uploading videos, managing comments, viewing analytics, configuring monetization, and accessing tools like Ask Studio and Creator Partnerships.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-studio/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-trends-tab/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Trends Tab</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A channel-level section of YouTube Analytics that surfaces top searches, Breakout videos from similar creators, Recent videos, and Shorts content gaps to help creators develop ideas. Updated with a new interface that began rolling out in July 2026.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-trends-tab/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-trim-tool/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Trim Tool</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Studio Editor feature that removes the beginning, end, or middle sections of an already uploaded video while preserving its URL, view count, and comments. Saved trims cannot be undone through Revert to original as of June 2025.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-trim-tool/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/youtube-view/" class="glossary-card-term">YouTube Views</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A count of how many times a video has been watched. For long-form videos, a view requires several seconds of watching; for Shorts (since March 2025), any play or scroll-by counts regardless of duration — making raw Shorts view counts and engaged views distinct metrics.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/youtube-view/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

      </div>

      <div class="glossary-category" id="production-editing">
        <h2 class="glossary-category-heading">Production &amp; Editing</h2>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">A</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/a-roll/" class="glossary-card-term">A-Roll</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The primary on-camera footage in a video — the creator talking to the lens, presenting information, or narrating. A-roll is the foundation of most talking-head and tutorial formats; B-roll is layered on top of it during editing.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/a-roll/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/acoustic-treatment/" class="glossary-card-term">Acoustic Treatment</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Physical materials (foam panels, bass traps, diffusers) placed in a recording space to reduce echo, reverb, and background noise. Acoustic treatment dramatically improves audio quality without requiring expensive microphone upgrades.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/acoustic-treatment/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/aperture/" class="glossary-card-term">Aperture</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The size of the opening in a camera lens that controls how much light reaches the sensor. A wider aperture (lower f-number) creates background blur and works better in low light; a narrower aperture keeps more of the scene in sharp focus.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/aperture/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/aspect-ratio/" class="glossary-card-term">Aspect Ratio</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The proportional relationship between a video's width and height. 16:9 is standard for YouTube long-form videos; 9:16 is vertical for Shorts. Using the wrong aspect ratio results in unwanted black bars or cropped content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/aspect-ratio/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">B</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/batch-editing/" class="glossary-card-term">Batch Editing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A production workflow that groups similar editing tasks — ingesting footage, cutting audio, adding captions, exporting — across several videos in one session to reduce setup switching. Also refers to YouTube Studio's bulk-change tool for updating titles, descriptions, visibility, or monetization settings on multiple uploads at once.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/batch-editing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/batch-filming/" class="glossary-card-term">Batch Filming</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A production method where a creator records several videos, Shorts, or segments during one planned session to reuse camera setup, lighting, location, and crew time. YouTube explicitly recommends it to make consistent publishing more sustainable — though it saves setup time, not script quality or editing effort.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/batch-filming/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">C</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/camera-angle/" class="glossary-card-term">Camera Angle</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The camera's viewpoint and orientation relative to the subject — eye level, high, low, overhead, ground level, or Dutch — determining which surfaces are visible, how the background is arranged, and how the audience experiences the action.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/camera-angle/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/chroma-key/" class="glossary-card-term">Chroma Key</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The technique of shooting a subject in front of a solid-color background (usually green or blue) so that color can be digitally removed in post and replaced with any other image or video. Also called green screen compositing.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/chroma-key/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/close-up/" class="glossary-card-term">Close-Up</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A tightly framed camera shot that makes a face, object, or detail occupy most of the image, reducing surrounding context so the audience focuses on expression, texture, or information that might be missed in a wider shot.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/close-up/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cold-open/" class="glossary-card-term">Cold Open</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An opening that begins immediately with content — action, a result, a question, or a compelling scene — before channel branding, a formal host introduction, or normal setup. YouTube's official creator guidance has specifically recommended cold opens as one way to attract viewers in the first few seconds.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cold-open/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/color-correction/" class="glossary-card-term">Color Correction</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The editing process of adjusting a video's colors to be technically accurate — fixing white balance, exposure, and skin tones so footage looks natural and consistent before any stylized grading is applied.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/color-correction/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/color-grading/" class="glossary-card-term">Color Grading</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The creative process of stylizing a video's color palette to achieve a specific aesthetic look or mood, applied after color correction. Color grading gives videos a cinematic or distinctive feel beyond what was captured on camera.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/color-grading/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/color-temperature/" class="glossary-card-term">Color Temperature</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A measure of how warm (orange) or cool (blue) a light source appears, measured in Kelvin. Matching color temperature across multiple light sources prevents inconsistent, mixed-color footage in a studio video setup.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/color-temperature/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cutaway/" class="glossary-card-term">Cutaway</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A supplementary shot that temporarily leaves the main action to show a related person, object, reaction, or location, then returns to the primary footage. Used to hide edits, add context, illustrate narration, and control pacing.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cutaway/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">D</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/depth-of-field/" class="glossary-card-term">Depth of Field</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The range of distance in a shot that appears acceptably sharp. A shallow depth of field produces a blurred background (bokeh) for a cinematic look; a deep depth of field keeps the full frame in focus.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/depth-of-field/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/dynamic-range/" class="glossary-card-term">Dynamic Range</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The difference between the brightest and darkest areas a camera can capture simultaneously without losing detail. Higher dynamic range footage retains more information in both highlights and shadows, giving editors more flexibility in post.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/dynamic-range/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">E</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/encoding/" class="glossary-card-term">Encoding</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The process of converting raw video footage into a compressed digital file format optimized for playback, streaming, or upload. Common YouTube upload formats include H.264 and H.265, with MP4 as the typical container.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/encoding/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/exposure-triangle/" class="glossary-card-term">Exposure Triangle</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The relationship between three camera settings — aperture, shutter speed, and ISO — that together determine how bright or dark an image appears. Adjusting any one of the three always affects the other two.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/exposure-triangle/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">F</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/frame-rate-fps/" class="glossary-card-term">Frame Rate (FPS)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The number of individual frames captured per second in a video. 24 FPS gives a cinematic look; 30 FPS is standard for web content; 60 FPS produces smoother motion, commonly used for gaming and action footage.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/frame-rate-fps/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">G</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/gain-staging/" class="glossary-card-term">Gain Staging</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The practice of setting appropriate audio signal levels at each step of the recording and editing chain to maximize sound quality while avoiding distortion or background noise buildup in the final mix.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/gain-staging/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/green-screen/" class="glossary-card-term">Green Screen</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A bright green backdrop used in video production that can be digitally removed and replaced with any image or footage using chroma key compositing. Green is used because it's the color farthest from most human skin tones.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/green-screen/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">H</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/headroom/" class="glossary-card-term">Headroom</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The visible space between the top of a person's head and the upper frame edge. Too much makes the subject feel low or disconnected; too little feels cramped unless a deliberate close-up.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/headroom/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">I</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/iso/" class="glossary-card-term">ISO</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera setting controlling sensor sensitivity to light. Higher ISO brightens footage in dark environments but introduces visible grain (noise). Lower ISO produces cleaner images but requires more light to achieve proper exposure.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/iso/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">J</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/j-cut/" class="glossary-card-term">J-Cut</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An editing technique where audio from the next scene begins before its video appears on screen. The audio leads the visual cut, creating a smooth, cinematic transition that feels less abrupt than a standard straight cut.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/j-cut/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/jump-cut/" class="glossary-card-term">Jump Cut</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An editing technique that cuts between two shots of the same subject from slightly different angles or at different moments, creating an intentional visual "jump." Widely used on YouTube to maintain pace and remove dead space.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/jump-cut/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">K</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/keyframes/" class="glossary-card-term">Keyframes</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Points in a video editing timeline that define the start and end values of an animation or effect, with the software automatically creating the in-between frames. Keyframes enable smooth motion graphics, transitions, and dynamic visual effects.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/keyframes/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">L</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/l-cut/" class="glossary-card-term">L-Cut</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An editing technique where the video from the next scene begins while the previous scene's audio continues briefly. Keeps audio continuity intact while cutting forward visually, creating a layered, seamless transition.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/l-cut/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/lower-third/" class="glossary-card-term">Lower Third</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A graphic overlay placed in the lower portion of the screen displaying text such as a speaker's name, title, or caption. Common in interviews and news-style videos to identify who is speaking without interrupting the visual composition.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/lower-third/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/lut/" class="glossary-card-term">LUT (Look-Up Table)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A preset color profile applied to footage during editing to instantly transform its look and tone. LUTs enable consistent color grading across multiple clips and are widely used to match a specific cinematic style or aesthetic.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/lut/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">M</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/medium-shot/" class="glossary-card-term">Medium Shot</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera shot showing a person from approximately the waist upward, balancing facial expression and hand gestures with enough background for context. Common in interviews, tutorials, reviews, and talking-head presentations.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/medium-shot/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/motion-graphics/" class="glossary-card-term">Motion Graphics</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Animated design elements — text, shapes, logos, or illustrations — added to a video to inform, emphasize, or decorate. Used in intros, transitions, lower thirds, and explainer-style content to make visuals dynamic and engaging.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/motion-graphics/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">N</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/noise-floor/" class="glossary-card-term">Noise Floor</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The baseline level of background hiss, hum, or room tone present in an audio recording even when no one is speaking. A high noise floor makes a recording sound unprofessional and is difficult to fully remove in post-production.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/noise-floor/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">O</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/overhead-shot/" class="glossary-card-term">Overhead Shot</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A shot filmed with the camera positioned directly above the subject and aimed downward, creating a top-down view of surface arrangements and actions. Common in cooking, craft, tutorial, product layout, and unboxing content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/overhead-shot/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">P</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/pattern-interrupt/" class="glossary-card-term">Pattern Interrupt</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A deliberate change in a video's visual, audio, pacing, or narrative flow — such as cutting to B-roll, adding a diagram, changing music, or asking a question — intended to refresh viewer attention after one pattern has continued too long. A creator-strategy term, not an official YouTube metric; retention data can show where viewers stopped watching but cannot prove a specific editing change caused the result.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/pattern-interrupt/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/phantom-power/" class="glossary-card-term">Phantom Power</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A 48V electrical current sent through an XLR cable to power condenser microphones that can't operate without external power. Most audio interfaces supply phantom power via a switch labeled "+48V."</p>
  <a href="/glossary/phantom-power/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/point-of-view-shot/" class="glossary-card-term">Point-of-View Shot (POV)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A shot that presents the scene from the visual perspective of a defined character or participant, making the audience see what that observer sees. Established through editing: viewers see the observer look, then see the object or action from their position.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/point-of-view-shot/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/product-demonstration-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Product Demonstration Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video that shows how a product, software tool, or service performs through actual use — presenting the task, demonstrating the steps, and showing the real result. Distinct from a review, which evaluates rather than demonstrates.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/product-demonstration-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/proxy-files/" class="glossary-card-term">Proxy Files</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Lower-resolution copies of high-resolution video files used during editing to reduce processing demands on a computer. When editing is complete, proxy files are swapped back to the originals for the final full-resolution export.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/proxy-files/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">R</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/rendering/" class="glossary-card-term">Rendering</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The process a video editing program uses to process and output a finished edit as a new video file, applying all effects, transitions, and color work. Render times depend on video length, effects complexity, and hardware performance.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/rendering/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/rule-of-thirds/" class="glossary-card-term">Rule of Thirds</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A composition guideline that divides the frame into nine equal sections with two horizontal and two vertical lines, using the lines and their four intersections as reference points for placing subjects, eyes, horizons, and products.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/rule-of-thirds/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">S</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/screen-recording/" class="glossary-card-term">Screen Recording</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The process of capturing computer or display activity as a video file, covering an entire monitor, a window, a browser tab, or a selected region, with separate controls for microphone, system, and application audio.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/screen-recording/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shot-list/" class="glossary-card-term">Shot List</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A production-planning document that identifies the individual shots needed to film a video — including framing, angle, movement, audio, gear, and priority — to prevent missing coverage and organize filming efficiently.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shot-list/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shutter-speed/" class="glossary-card-term">Shutter Speed</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera setting controlling how long the sensor is exposed per frame. The "180-degree rule" recommends a shutter speed double the frame rate (e.g., 1/60 for 30 FPS) to produce natural-looking motion blur.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shutter-speed/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/stock-footage/" class="glossary-card-term">Stock Footage</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Pre-recorded video clips licensed for use in productions without filming them yourself. Used in YouTube videos to illustrate topics, add visual variety, or fill scenes the creator couldn't capture firsthand.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/stock-footage/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/storyboard/" class="glossary-card-term">Storyboard</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A sequence of visual panels showing how a video will unfold, with each panel representing a key shot, action, or transition. Helps plan composition, camera movement, continuity, and pacing before production begins.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/storyboard/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">T</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/talking-head-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Talking-Head Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video format where a person speaks on camera as the main information source, typically framed from the chest upward. The format allows for B-roll, graphics, jump cuts, and multiple angles while the on-camera speaker remains the primary focus.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/talking-head-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/teleprompter/" class="glossary-card-term">Teleprompter</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A device or app that displays a scrolling script in front of a camera lens so creators can read their lines while appearing to look directly into the camera. Useful for scripted content requiring word-for-word delivery.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/teleprompter/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/three-point-lighting/" class="glossary-card-term">Three-Point Lighting</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The foundational studio lighting setup using a key light (main), fill light (reduces shadows), and back light (separates subject from background). The standard starting point for professional-looking YouTube video production.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/three-point-lighting/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/timeline/" class="glossary-card-term">Timeline</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">In video editing software, the visual workspace where creators arrange video clips, audio tracks, transitions, and effects in sequence. The primary working area of any non-linear video editing program.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/timeline/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/transcoding/" class="glossary-card-term">Transcoding</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The process of converting a video file from one format, codec, or bitrate to another. YouTube automatically transcodes uploaded videos into multiple resolutions to enable adaptive streaming across different devices and connection speeds.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/transcoding/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">V</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-bitrate/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Bitrate</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The amount of data used per second to store or stream video, measured in Mbps. Higher bitrates preserve more visual detail but produce larger file sizes. YouTube publishes recommended upload bitrates by resolution and frame rate.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-bitrate/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-codec/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Codec</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The compression algorithm used to encode and decode video data. H.264 is the most widely supported codec for YouTube uploads; H.265 and VP9 offer better quality at smaller file sizes but require more processing power.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-codec/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-framing/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Framing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The deliberate selection and arrangement of everything visible within the image boundary — including subject placement, headroom, look room, and negative space. Distinct from shot size and camera angle.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-framing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-outline/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Outline</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A structured plan organizing the promise, hook, main sections, evidence, visuals, transitions, and call to action of a YouTube video before filming begins. Sits between a content brief and a full script — faster to prepare than a word-for-word script but structured enough to prevent omissions, repeated takes, and editing confusion.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-outline/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-resolution/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Resolution</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The number of pixels in each frame of a video (e.g., 1920×1080 for 1080p, 3840×2160 for 4K). Higher resolution means sharper image quality but larger files and longer upload and processing times on YouTube.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-resolution/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/voice-over/" class="glossary-card-term">Voice-Over</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A recorded narration track added to a video where the speaker is heard but not seen on camera. Common in tutorials, explainer videos, and faceless channels where audio narration guides the viewer through visual content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/voice-over/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">W</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/white-balance/" class="glossary-card-term">White Balance</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera setting that adjusts how white appears on screen to look neutral, compensating for the color cast of different light sources. Correct white balance prevents footage from looking too orange (warm) or blue (cool).</p>
  <a href="/glossary/white-balance/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/wide-shot/" class="glossary-card-term">Wide Shot</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera shot that shows a subject with substantial surrounding environment. When the subject is a person, the full body typically appears alongside enough location to show where they are and how they relate to the space.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/wide-shot/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

      </div>

      <div class="glossary-category" id="brand-deals">
        <h2 class="glossary-category-heading">Brand Deals &amp; Sponsorships</h2>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">A</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/affiliate-commission/" class="glossary-card-term">Affiliate Commission</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The percentage or flat fee a creator earns each time a viewer completes a qualifying action — typically a purchase — through their unique affiliate link. Commission rates vary widely by program, niche, and product type.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/affiliate-commission/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/affiliate-link/" class="glossary-card-term">Affiliate Link</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A unique URL assigned to a creator that tracks purchases or signups from their content. When a viewer clicks the link and completes a transaction, the creator earns an affiliate commission from the brand or network.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/affiliate-link/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/affiliate-marketing/" class="glossary-card-term">Affiliate Marketing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A revenue model where creators earn commissions by promoting companies' products through unique tracking links. Popular because it requires no upfront cost, scales with traffic, and works alongside ad revenue and sponsorships.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/affiliate-marketing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/affiliate-network/" class="glossary-card-term">Affiliate Network</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A marketplace platform (like ShareASale, Impact, or Amazon Associates) connecting creators with multiple brands' affiliate programs in one place, handling link tracking, reporting, and commission payments centrally.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/affiliate-network/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/affiliate-program/" class="glossary-card-term">Affiliate Program</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A brand's own structured system for recruiting and paying affiliates who drive sales or leads. Some brands run proprietary programs independently; others use third-party affiliate networks to manage creator partnerships at scale.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/affiliate-program/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/approval-process/" class="glossary-card-term">Approval Process</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The review cycle in a brand deal where a sponsor reviews a creator's draft content — script, video edit, or post — and either approves it, requests changes, or rejects it before the creator is permitted to publish.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/approval-process/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/attribution/" class="glossary-card-term">Attribution</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The process of determining which channel, link, or creator drove a specific action like a purchase or signup. Brands use attribution to measure campaign ROI and decide which creator partnerships to renew or scale.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/attribution/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/audience-demographics/" class="glossary-card-term">Audience Demographics</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Data on a creator's viewers — age, gender, location, and interests. Brands evaluate audience demographics when deciding whether a creator's followers match the brand's target customer profile.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/audience-demographics/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/audience-fit/" class="glossary-card-term">Audience Fit</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">How well a creator's audience aligns with a brand's target customer. Good audience fit is the most important factor in a successful sponsorship — poor fit produces low conversions even with large view counts.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/audience-fit/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">B</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/brand-affinity/" class="glossary-card-term">Brand Affinity</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The degree of positive connection a creator's audience feels toward a specific brand. High brand affinity means viewers already trust or like the brand, making creator endorsements more effective and natural for both parties.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/brand-affinity/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/brand-deal/" class="glossary-card-term">Brand Deal</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A paid partnership between a creator and a company where the creator produces content featuring or promoting the brand's product in exchange for payment, free products, or revenue share. The primary income source for many mid-to-large channels.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/brand-deal/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">C</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/campaign-brief/" class="glossary-card-term">Campaign Brief</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A document from a brand outlining the goals, requirements, messaging, deliverables, and timeline for a sponsored content partnership. Creators use the brief to understand exactly what they must produce before signing a contract.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/campaign-brief/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/category-exclusivity/" class="glossary-card-term">Category Exclusivity</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A contract clause preventing a creator from working with competing brands in the same product category during a set period — for example, agreeing not to promote any other VPN service for six months after a deal.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/category-exclusivity/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/channel-portfolio/" class="glossary-card-term">Channel Portfolio</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The full collection of YouTube channels and social accounts a creator or creator network offers to brands for sponsorship placements. Larger portfolios give creators leverage in pitching multi-platform deals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/channel-portfolio/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/click-attribution/" class="glossary-card-term">Click Attribution</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A model that credits a conversion to the last link a customer clicked before completing an action. The most common attribution model in affiliate marketing because it's straightforward to track via affiliate links.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/click-attribution/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-licensing/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Licensing</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The formal permission granted by a creator allowing a brand to use their video content in the brand's own marketing, ads, or channels, typically in exchange for a licensing fee separate from the original creation payment.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-licensing/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/content-ownership/" class="glossary-card-term">Content Ownership</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The legal rights to content once created. In most creator-brand deals, the creator retains ownership unless the contract explicitly transfers copyright. Work-made-for-hire arrangements can shift full ownership to the commissioning brand.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/content-ownership/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/conversion-rate/" class="glossary-card-term">Conversion Rate</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The percentage of viewers who take a desired action (purchasing, signing up, downloading) after seeing sponsored content. Higher conversion rates indicate stronger audience trust and better alignment between the creator and brand.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/conversion-rate/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/conversion-tracking/" class="glossary-card-term">Conversion Tracking</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The technical process of monitoring specific actions taken by viewers after clicking a creator's affiliate link or promo code — typically purchases or signups — to measure a campaign's actual performance.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/conversion-tracking/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cost-per-acquisition/" class="glossary-card-term">Cost per Acquisition (CPA)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The amount a brand pays per confirmed conversion or customer acquired through a creator's campaign. A performance-based metric that shifts some financial risk from brand to creator compared to flat-fee sponsorship deals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cost-per-acquisition/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cost-per-engagement/" class="glossary-card-term">Cost per Engagement (CPE)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The amount a brand pays per viewer action — like a like, comment, or click — on sponsored content. CPE campaigns prioritize audience interaction quality rather than raw impressions or view totals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cost-per-engagement/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cost-per-mille-cpm/" class="glossary-card-term">Cost per Mille/CPM</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">In sponsorship deals, the amount a brand pays per 1,000 impressions of sponsored content. Used to price and compare deals across creators of different sizes, separate from YouTube's internal ad revenue CPM.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cost-per-mille-cpm/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cost-per-view/" class="glossary-card-term">Cost per View (CPV)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The amount a brand pays per video view generated by a sponsored placement. CPV models align brand investment directly with viewership and are common in performance-oriented video advertising campaigns.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cost-per-view/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creative-brief/" class="glossary-card-term">Creative Brief</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A more detailed version of a campaign brief, specifically outlining creative direction — tone, visual style, messaging dos and don'ts, and examples — to guide a creator's content production for a sponsored campaign.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creative-brief/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-economy/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Economy</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The broader ecosystem of independent creators monetizing content, audiences, and expertise across platforms. Encompasses ad revenue, brand deals, memberships, merchandise, courses, and all other creator-driven revenue streams.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-economy/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-media-kit/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Media Kit</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A document creators use to pitch themselves to brands, summarizing audience demographics, key engagement metrics, content niche, past partnerships, and sponsorship rates. The creator's primary sales and self-promotion document.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-media-kit/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-rate-card/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Rate Card</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A pricing document showing a creator's standard rates for different deliverables — dedicated videos, mentions, Instagram posts, Shorts — giving brands a clear starting point for negotiating sponsorship packages.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-rate-card/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-storefront/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Storefront</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A curated page where a creator showcases and links to products they recommend, earn affiliate commissions on, or sell directly to their audience — either through YouTube Shopping or a standalone link-in-bio page.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-storefront/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">D</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/deliverables/" class="glossary-card-term">Deliverables</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The specific content pieces a creator is contractually required to produce and publish for a brand deal — defined as specific video types, lengths, post formats, or quantities that must be delivered by an agreed deadline.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/deliverables/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/digital-product/" class="glossary-card-term">Digital Product</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A downloadable or online-access product a creator sells directly to their audience — presets, templates, courses, or e-books. High margins because there are no physical production or shipping costs once the product is created.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/digital-product/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">E</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/earned-media-value/" class="glossary-card-term">Earned Media Value (EMV)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An estimated dollar value assigned to organic creator content, calculated by comparing it to equivalent paid advertising costs. Brands use EMV to quantify the value of creator partnerships beyond direct conversion metrics.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/earned-media-value/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/engagement-rate/" class="glossary-card-term">Engagement Rate</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The percentage of a creator's audience that actively interacts with content through likes, comments, shares, or saves. Brands use engagement rate to gauge how connected and responsive a creator's audience actually is, beyond subscriber count.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/engagement-rate/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/exclusivity-clause/" class="glossary-card-term">Exclusivity Clause</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A contract term restricting a creator from working with competing brands in the same category for a defined period. Protects the sponsoring brand's investment but limits the creator's flexibility to accept other deals.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/exclusivity-clause/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">F</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ftc-sponsorship-disclosure/" class="glossary-card-term">FTC Sponsorship Disclosure</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A US legal requirement (under FTC Endorsement Guides) that creators clearly disclose when content is paid or sponsored. Must be visible upfront — not buried in descriptions. "Ad" or "Sponsored" are acceptable labels.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ftc-sponsorship-disclosure/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">K</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/kill-fee/" class="glossary-card-term">Kill Fee</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A contractual payment made to a creator if a brand cancels a project after work has begun or been completed. Protects creators from losing time and out-of-pocket expenses when a brand pulls out unexpectedly.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/kill-fee/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">L</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/late-fee/" class="glossary-card-term">Late Fee</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A penalty charge built into a creator-brand contract that the brand owes if payment is not received by the agreed due date. Creates financial accountability and encourages brands to pay on time.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/late-fee/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">M</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/merch-shelf/" class="glossary-card-term">Merch Shelf</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube Shopping feature that lets creators display and sell their own merchandise directly below their videos. Eligible Partner Program creators link a connected store to surface products to viewers without leaving YouTube.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/merch-shelf/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/merchandising/" class="glossary-card-term">Merchandising</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The design, production, and sale of physical products — apparel, accessories, prints — using a creator's brand or imagery. A major secondary revenue stream for creators with strong brand identity and a loyal audience willing to spend.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/merchandising/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/morality-clause/" class="glossary-card-term">Morality Clause</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A contract clause allowing a brand to terminate a partnership if a creator engages in behavior the brand deems harmful to its reputation. Scope is often broad and can cover past actions discovered after the contract is signed.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/morality-clause/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">P</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/paid-usage/" class="glossary-card-term">Paid Usage</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A contract clause granting the brand rights to use a creator's content in paid advertising, often at an additional fee beyond the base sponsorship rate. Expands where and how long the brand can run the creator's content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/paid-usage/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/partnership-ads/" class="glossary-card-term">Partnership Ads</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube advertising format that lets brands run a creator's sponsored content as a paid in-stream or Shorts ad — with the creator's permission — to amplify reach beyond the creator's organic audience.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/partnership-ads/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/passive-income/" class="glossary-card-term">Passive Income</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Revenue that continues without ongoing active work — ad revenue from an existing video catalog, affiliate links in older videos, and digital product sales all represent passive income streams for creators.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/passive-income/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/patreon-membership-model/" class="glossary-card-term">Patreon/Membership Model</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A direct fan-support system where viewers pay a monthly fee for perks like exclusive content, early access, or community access. Patreon is a third-party platform; YouTube's equivalent is Channel Memberships.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/patreon-membership-model/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/payment-terms/" class="glossary-card-term">Payment Terms</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The contractual agreement between a creator and brand specifying when and how payment will be made — typically net-30 or net-60 days after delivery. A key negotiation point that directly affects a creator's cash flow.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/payment-terms/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/perpetual-usage-rights/" class="glossary-card-term">Perpetual Usage Rights</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A clause granting a brand unlimited, ongoing rights to use a creator's content forever with no expiration date. Significantly more valuable than time-limited usage rights and should command meaningfully higher compensation.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/perpetual-usage-rights/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/promo-code/" class="glossary-card-term">Promo Code</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A unique discount code a creator shares with their audience, used at checkout. Brands track how many sales originated from each creator's code and sometimes pay creators a commission on sales driven.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/promo-code/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">R</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/recurring-revenue/" class="glossary-card-term">Recurring Revenue</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Income that arrives on a predictable, ongoing basis — channel memberships, Patreon subscriptions, and retainer-based brand partnerships are all recurring revenue that gives creators financial stability month to month.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/recurring-revenue/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/referral-program/" class="glossary-card-term">Referral Program</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A structure where a brand rewards creators or customers for bringing in new buyers. Creators participate by sharing referral links or codes that track new signups or purchases they generate for the brand.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/referral-program/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/return-on-ad-spend/" class="glossary-card-term">Return on Ad Spend (ROAS)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A metric brands use to measure revenue generated for every dollar spent on advertising, including creator sponsorships. A ROAS of 3x means the brand earned $3 for every $1 spent on creator campaigns.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/return-on-ad-spend/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/return-on-investment/" class="glossary-card-term">Return on Investment (ROI)</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A broad measure of profit relative to cost. In creator partnerships, brands calculate ROI by comparing campaign results — sales, brand lift, awareness — against total sponsorship spend including creator fees.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/return-on-investment/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/revenue-share/" class="glossary-card-term">Revenue Share</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A monetization model where a creator earns a percentage of the revenue their promotion generates rather than a flat fee. Common in affiliate programs, some brand deals, and YouTube's own ad revenue split with Partner Program creators.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/revenue-share/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/revision-round/" class="glossary-card-term">Revision Round</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">One cycle of a creator submitting content for brand review and the brand providing feedback for changes. Contracts typically specify how many rounds are included before additional revisions cost extra.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/revision-round/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/right-of-first-refusal/" class="glossary-card-term">Right of First Refusal</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A clause giving a brand priority to renew or continue a partnership before the creator negotiates with a competing brand. Protects the existing relationship but limits the creator's ability to solicit competing offers.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/right-of-first-refusal/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">S</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sponsored-content/" class="glossary-card-term">Sponsored Content</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Any video, post, or piece of content a creator was paid to produce on behalf of a brand. Must be disclosed to viewers under FTC guidelines and YouTube's own policies, typically with an upfront "paid promotion" label.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sponsored-content/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sponsored-video/" class="glossary-card-term">Sponsored Video</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A YouTube video fully funded by a brand, where the entire video is created in partnership with the sponsor rather than featuring a short mention or integrated segment within the creator's regular content format.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sponsored-video/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sponsorship/" class="glossary-card-term">Sponsorship</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A commercial arrangement where a brand pays a creator to feature, mention, or promote their product within the creator's content. Ranges from brief mid-video mentions to full dedicated sponsorship videos with multiple deliverables.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sponsorship/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sponsorship-compensation/" class="glossary-card-term">Sponsorship Compensation</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The total payment a creator receives for a brand deal, which may include a flat creative fee, performance bonuses, free products, affiliate commissions, or any combination of these elements.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sponsorship-compensation/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sponsorship-disclosure/" class="glossary-card-term">Sponsorship Disclosure</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A creator's required, clear communication to their audience that content has been paid for by a brand. Must be visible upfront — not buried in the description — under FTC guidelines in the US and similar regulations globally.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sponsorship-disclosure/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">T</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/tracking-link/" class="glossary-card-term">Tracking Link</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A URL embedded with parameters that identify the creator as the source of traffic or conversions. When a viewer clicks the link, the brand attributes any resulting sales or signups to that specific creator's campaign.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/tracking-link/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">U</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/usage-rights/" class="glossary-card-term">Usage Rights</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The specific permissions a creator grants a brand to use their content — defining where, for how long, and in what formats. Limited usage rights (e.g., 60-day social use) are standard; broader or perpetual rights require additional compensation.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/usage-rights/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/utm-parameters/" class="glossary-card-term">UTM Parameters</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Tags appended to URLs that track where website traffic originated. Brands add UTM parameters to creator links to identify which creator, campaign, and content format drove the most conversions in their analytics.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/utm-parameters/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">V</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/view-through-attribution/" class="glossary-card-term">View-Through Attribution</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A model that credits a conversion to a creator's content even if the viewer never clicked a link, assuming the brand impression influenced the eventual purchase. Harder to measure and more debated than click-based attribution.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/view-through-attribution/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="glossary-letter">W</h3>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/whitelisting/" class="glossary-card-term">Whitelisting</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A process where a creator grants a brand permission to run paid ads through the creator's own YouTube channel or social account. The brand manages and funds the ad, which appears to come from the creator, extending reach while maintaining authenticity.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/whitelisting/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/work-made-for-hire/" class="glossary-card-term">Work Made for Hire</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A legal arrangement where the brand commissions content and immediately owns the copyright, rather than the creator retaining ownership and licensing usage. Must be explicitly stated in writing — it does not apply by default.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/work-made-for-hire/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>

      </div>

      <div class="glossary-category" id="creator-equipment">
        <h2 class="glossary-category-heading">Creator Equipment</h2>
        <ul class="glossary-term-list">
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/3-2-1-backup-rule/" class="glossary-card-term">3-2-1 Backup Rule</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A data-protection guideline calling for three total copies of important files across two different storage types, with one copy kept off-site. Reduces single points of failure from device loss, location-wide events, and ransomware.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/3-2-1-backup-rule/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/action-camera/" class="glossary-card-term">Action Cameras</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Compact, rugged cameras (like GoPro) designed for capturing footage in challenging or active environments. Key features include wide-angle lenses, waterproofing, and built-in stabilization for hands-free mounting during outdoor or sports content.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/action-camera/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/aps-c-camera/" class="glossary-card-term">APS-C Camera</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera using a sensor smaller than full frame with a crop factor of about 1.5× or 1.6×, offering compact size, affordable lenses, forgiving focus depth, and strong video quality — a popular choice for YouTubers at every level.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/aps-c-camera/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/audio-clipping/" class="glossary-card-term">Audio Clipping</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Distortion that occurs when an audio signal exceeds the maximum level a device or recording stage can handle cleanly, causing waveform peaks to be flattened rather than reproduced accurately. Severe clipping is difficult to repair in post.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/audio-clipping/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/audio-interface/" class="glossary-card-term">Audio Interface</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A device that connects microphones to a computer, converting analog audio to digital for recording. Required for XLR microphones, which can't plug directly into a standard computer's headphone or USB jack.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/audio-interface/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/autofocus/" class="glossary-card-term">Autofocus</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera system that automatically adjusts the lens to keep a subject sharp, using face detection, eye tracking, and continuous modes to help solo YouTube creators stay in focus without manual adjustment.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/autofocus/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/bi-color-light/" class="glossary-card-term">Bi-Color Light</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A video light that blends warm and cool LED emitters to produce adjustable white light across a color temperature range. Allows creators to match window light, household lamps, or a deliberate studio look without color-correction gels.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/bi-color-light/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/boom-arm/" class="glossary-card-term">Boom Arm</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An adjustable desk-mounted support that positions a microphone close to the creator while keeping the desk clear. Allows fast repositioning between speaking, typing, and on-camera moments without touching the microphone.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/boom-arm/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/camcorders/" class="glossary-card-term">Camcorders</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Dedicated video recording devices with built-in optics, longer zoom ranges, and features optimized for continuous recording. Popular for event videography, travel content, and creators who prioritize ease of use over interchangeable lenses.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/camcorders/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/camera-battery/" class="glossary-card-term">Camera Battery</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A removable rechargeable lithium-ion power source that supplies electricity to a camera and its systems. Understanding voltage, capacity, OEM versus third-party compatibility, USB charging, and travel rules helps creators plan for long shoots.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/camera-battery/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/camera-lens/" class="glossary-card-term">Camera Lens</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The optical component that gathers and focuses light onto the camera sensor, shaping framing, background blur, low-light performance, and autofocus behavior for every video a creator shoots.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/camera-lens/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/camera-sensor/" class="glossary-card-term">Camera Sensor</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The electronic component that converts light from the lens into image data, determining resolution, field of view, low-light performance, dynamic range, rolling shutter, and autofocus design.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/camera-sensor/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/capture-card/" class="glossary-card-term">Capture Card</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A device that receives a video signal from a camera, game console, or computer and converts it into a feed that recording or streaming software can use. Available as external USB/Thunderbolt devices or internal PCIe cards, with separate input, capture, and passthrough specifications.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/capture-card/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/cardioid-microphone/" class="glossary-card-term">Cardioid Microphone</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A microphone that captures sound primarily from the front and rejects the greatest amount from directly behind it. The most common polar pattern for solo desk recording, podcasting, and streaming because it helps reduce keyboard and background noise.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/cardioid-microphone/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/clean-hdmi/" class="glossary-card-term">Clean HDMI</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera's HDMI output with menus, focus boxes, battery icons, and other interface graphics removed so a clean picture can feed a capture card, monitor, recorder, or video switcher. Does not guarantee uncompressed video, 4K output, unlimited runtime, embedded audio, or continuous autofocus.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/clean-hdmi/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/condenser-microphones/" class="glossary-card-term">Condenser Microphones</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Highly sensitive microphones that excel at capturing detailed, transparent sound in controlled studio environments. They require phantom power and are ideal for voice-overs and studio recordings but more susceptible to picking up room noise.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/condenser-microphones/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/creator-backup/" class="glossary-card-term">Creator Backup</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A separate recoverable copy of files and information needed to continue producing after a loss event — covering raw footage, project files, exports, licenses, and channel data a creator cannot easily recreate.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/creator-backup/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/crop-factor/" class="glossary-card-term">Crop Factor</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A number comparing a camera sensor to a 35mm full-frame sensor, used to calculate equivalent focal length and understand how the same lens will frame a scene differently on APS-C versus full-frame cameras.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/crop-factor/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/desktop-tripod/" class="glossary-card-term">Desktop Tripod</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A short three-legged support designed to stand on a desk, table, or shelf for webcams, smartphones, compact cameras, and lights. Performs the same stabilization job as a full-size tripod but depends on furniture for working height.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/desktop-tripod/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/dslr-cameras/" class="glossary-card-term">DSLR Cameras</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Digital single-lens reflex cameras offering interchangeable lenses, large sensors, and strong video quality, originally designed for photography. A long-popular choice for YouTube creators wanting cinematic image quality at accessible price points.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/dslr-cameras/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/dual-pc-streaming/" class="glossary-card-term">Dual-PC Streaming</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A production setup that uses one computer for gaming or a demanding application and a second computer for streaming, encoding, overlays, and recording. Separates workloads but adds capture hardware, audio routing, and more points of failure than a single-PC setup.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/dual-pc-streaming/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/dummy-battery/" class="glossary-card-term">Dummy Battery</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A battery-shaped power coupler (also called a DC coupler) that fits inside a camera's battery compartment and supplies continuous power from an external adapter. Used for livestreams, studio sessions, and long recordings where swapping batteries would interrupt the feed.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/dummy-battery/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/dynamic-microphones/" class="glossary-card-term">Dynamic Microphones</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Rugged microphones that reject background noise and room acoustics well, making them practical for home studios and streaming in untreated spaces. They don't require phantom power and handle loud sound sources without distortion.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/dynamic-microphones/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/external-hard-drive/" class="glossary-card-term">External Hard Drive</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A hard disk drive in an external enclosure that connects through USB or Thunderbolt. Offers large capacities at a lower cost per terabyte than solid-state drives, making it a practical choice for backups, archives, and large media libraries.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/external-hard-drive/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/external-ssd/" class="glossary-card-term">External SSD</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A solid-state storage device that connects outside a computer through USB or Thunderbolt. Faster and quieter than external hard drives, commonly used for active editing projects, rapid media transfers, and portable high-bitrate recording.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/external-ssd/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/eye-autofocus/" class="glossary-card-term">Eye Autofocus</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera feature that detects a subject's eye and keeps focus precisely on it, especially valuable for solo creators recording with a wide aperture where small focus errors become visible.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/eye-autofocus/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/focal-length/" class="glossary-card-term">Focal Length</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">The optical measurement in millimeters that determines how wide or narrow a lens sees, controlling angle of view, subject magnification, working distance, and how much of a room fits in the frame.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/focal-length/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/full-frame-camera/" class="glossary-card-term">Full-Frame Camera</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera with a sensor approximately 36 × 24mm, the same size as a 35mm film frame, offering wide fields of view, shallow depth-of-field potential, and strong low-light performance compared to smaller-sensor formats.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/full-frame-camera/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/gimbal/" class="glossary-card-term">Gimbal</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A motorized stabilization device that holds a camera and uses sensors and motors to counteract hand movement, producing smooth footage without the camera shake common in handheld shooting during walks, action, or travel.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/gimbal/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/headphone-monitoring/" class="glossary-card-term">Headphone Monitoring</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Listening to a microphone or playback signal through headphones during recording or streaming to catch clipping, dropouts, routing errors, and other audio problems before they become permanent in the recording.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/headphone-monitoring/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/image-stabilization/" class="glossary-card-term">Image Stabilization</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera or lens system that reduces visible shake from small movements using optical, in-body, or electronic correction — essential for handheld vlogging and walking shots where a tripod or gimbal isn't practical.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/image-stabilization/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/kit-lens/" class="glossary-card-term">Kit Lens</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera lens bundled with a camera body as a starter package, typically a compact zoom selected for affordability and general use, giving new creators a versatile starting point before upgrading for specific needs.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/kit-lens/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/lavalier-microphones/" class="glossary-card-term">Lavalier Microphones</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Small clip-on microphones that attach to clothing near the mouth, capturing clear audio while keeping the mic out of frame. Popular for interviews, run-and-gun vlogging, and mobile filming where on-camera mics aren't practical.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/lavalier-microphones/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/light-stand/" class="glossary-card-term">Light Stand</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">An adjustable support that holds video lights and lightweight accessories above the floor, allowing creators to position key, fill, and background lights without using furniture or improvised supports.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/light-stand/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/memory-card-reader/" class="glossary-card-term">Memory Card Reader</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A device that connects a memory card to a computer for file transfer without connecting the camera directly. Card format, bus interface, USB generation, and whether slots share bandwidth all affect how fast footage ingests.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/memory-card-reader/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/microphone-preamp/" class="glossary-card-term">Microphone Preamplifiers</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Devices that boost a microphone's weak output signal to a usable recording level. Built into most audio interfaces, but dedicated standalone preamps offer cleaner amplification that can noticeably improve recording quality for voice-over work.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/microphone-preamp/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/microphone-windscreen/" class="glossary-card-term">Microphone Windscreen</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A foam, furry, or blimp enclosure that fits over a microphone to reduce noise from wind, breath, movement, and air conditioning. Used indoors and outdoors, with foam for light conditions and fur-style "dead cat" covers for stronger wind.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/microphone-windscreen/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/mirrorless-camera/" class="glossary-card-term">Mirrorless Camera</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A compact interchangeable-lens camera that removes the traditional DSLR mirror mechanism, resulting in a lighter, quieter body with excellent video capabilities. Increasingly the preferred camera choice for serious YouTube content creators.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/mirrorless-camera/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/mono-vs-stereo-audio/" class="glossary-card-term">Mono vs. Stereo Audio</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Mono uses one audio signal; stereo uses distinct left and right channels. Voice recording typically stays mono for consistent playback across all devices, while music and ambience often benefit from true stereo width.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/mono-vs-stereo-audio/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/natural-lighting/" class="glossary-card-term">Natural Lighting</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Illumination that comes from the sun — including direct sunlight, window light, open shade, and overcast daylight. Can produce soft, realistic-looking video without a lighting kit but changes with time of day, weather, and camera direction.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/natural-lighting/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/nd-filter/" class="glossary-card-term">ND Filter</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera lens filter (Neutral Density) that reduces the amount of light entering the lens without affecting color. Allows creators to use a wider aperture or slower shutter speed in bright outdoor conditions while maintaining proper exposure.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/nd-filter/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/omnidirectional-microphone/" class="glossary-card-term">Omnidirectional Microphone</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A microphone that captures sound equally from all directions around the capsule. Common in lavalier and headset microphones because its broad pickup stays consistent even when the speaker turns their head.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/omnidirectional-microphone/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/optical-zoom-vs-digital-zoom/" class="glossary-card-term">Optical Zoom vs. Digital Zoom</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Optical zoom changes a lens's focal length to get closer to a subject, while digital zoom crops or enlarges image data — understanding the difference helps creators choose when each approach is appropriate.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/optical-zoom-vs-digital-zoom/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/overhead-camera-mount/" class="glossary-card-term">Overhead Camera Mount</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A support system that positions a camera or phone above a subject with the lens aimed downward for top-down views. Used for cooking videos, product shots, tutorials, unboxings, and any workflow requiring a bird's-eye-view frame.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/overhead-camera-mount/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/phone-mount/" class="glossary-card-term">Phone Mount</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A holder or adapter that secures a smartphone to a tripod, desk arm, cage, gimbal, or other support. Available as spring clamps, screw-tightened clamps, and magnetic systems, each requiring a matching support interface.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/phone-mount/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/phone-tripod/" class="glossary-card-term">Phone Tripod</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A three-legged support designed specifically for smartphones, ranging from pocket-size tabletop models to full-height stands. Includes or accepts a phone holder and enables hands-free recording without a camera operator.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/phone-tripod/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/polar-pattern/" class="glossary-card-term">Polar Pattern</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A diagram showing how sensitive a microphone is to sound arriving from different directions. Understanding polar patterns — cardioid, omnidirectional, figure-eight, and shotgun — helps creators choose and position a microphone correctly.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/polar-pattern/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/pop-filter/" class="glossary-card-term">Pop Filter</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A mesh or foam screen positioned between a speaker and microphone to disperse air bursts from plosive sounds (P, B, T, K) before they hit the capsule, preventing loud thumping artifacts in the recording.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/pop-filter/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/prime-lens/" class="glossary-card-term">Prime Lens</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera lens with one fixed focal length that cannot optically zoom, often offering a wider maximum aperture and more compact size than zoom lenses, making it popular for low-light recording and background blur.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/prime-lens/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/quick-release-plate/" class="glossary-card-term">Quick-Release Plate</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A small plate that attaches to a camera and locks into a matching clamp on a tripod head or other support, enabling fast mounting and removal without unscrewing the camera each time. Plate and receiver must be verified as compatible.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/quick-release-plate/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/rgb-light/" class="glossary-card-term">RGB Light</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A color-changing light that mixes red, green, and blue LED channels to create a wide range of hues. Used by creators for background separation, rim lighting, brand color accents, and special effects without needing separate gels.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/rgb-light/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/ring-light/" class="glossary-card-term">Ring Lights</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">Circular LED lights mounted around a camera lens that produce even, flattering front-facing illumination with a characteristic circular catchlight in the subject's eyes. Popular for beauty, talking-head, and studio-based YouTube setups.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/ring-light/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sd-card/" class="glossary-card-term">SD Card</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A compact removable flash-memory card used to store video, photos, and audio in cameras, recorders, and drones. Capacity standard, speed class, bus interface, and file system must all match the recording device's requirements.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sd-card/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sd-card-speed-class/" class="glossary-card-term">SD Card Speed Class</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A standardized rating indicating a card's minimum sustained sequential write speed — the metric that determines whether it can keep up with a camera's continuous recording. V, U, C, and E class symbols each represent a different performance floor.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sd-card-speed-class/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shock-mount/" class="glossary-card-term">Shock Mount</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A microphone holder that suspends or cushions the mic using elastic, rubber, or silicone to isolate it from vibrations traveling through a desk, boom arm, or stand. Prevents low-frequency rumble, keyboard thumps, and handling noise from reaching the recording.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shock-mount/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/shotgun-microphone/" class="glossary-card-term">Shotgun Microphone</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A highly directional microphone that captures audio primarily from the direction it points while rejecting side and rear noise. Often mounted on-camera or a boom pole for interviews, vlogging, and outdoor recording situations.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/shotgun-microphone/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/softbox/" class="glossary-card-term">Softbox</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A lighting modifier that diffuses light through a translucent panel to produce soft, even illumination with gradual shadows. Produces more flattering and professional-looking video lighting than bare LED panels or direct light sources.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/softbox/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/sound-card/" class="glossary-card-term">Sound Cards</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">External USB audio devices that add audio input and output capabilities to a computer, often marketed to streamers and podcasters for simple plug-and-play microphone connections without a full audio interface setup.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/sound-card/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/stream-deck/" class="glossary-card-term">Stream Deck</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A programmable control device by Elgato that uses customizable LCD keys, dials, and touch controls to trigger scene changes, mutes, recordings, alerts, and multi-step automations in connected software. Does not capture or process audio or video itself.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/stream-deck/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/tripod/" class="glossary-card-term">Tripod</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A three-legged camera support that eliminates hand shake, keeps framing consistent between takes, and allows solo creators to appear on camera without an operator. Video tripods with fluid heads also enable smooth pans and tilts.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/tripod/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/usb-microphone/" class="glossary-card-term">USB Microphone</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A microphone that connects directly to a computer via USB, requiring no audio interface. Convenient for beginners and ideal for solo voice-over work, podcasting, and basic streaming where simplicity is more important than maximum audio control.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/usb-microphone/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/video-switcher/" class="glossary-card-term">Video Switcher</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A device or software system that selects between multiple cameras and media sources and combines them into one live program output. Used to cut between cameras, apply transitions, add graphics, and create picture-in-picture layouts during a livestream or multi-camera event.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/video-switcher/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/virtual-camera/" class="glossary-card-term">Virtual Camera</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A software-generated video source that appears to other applications as a physical webcam, letting creators send a fully composed scene — with cameras, screens, graphics, and overlays — into meeting apps, recording tools, and streaming services.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/virtual-camera/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/webcams/" class="glossary-card-term">Webcams</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">External cameras that connect to a computer via USB, designed primarily for video calls and live streaming. Offer plug-and-play simplicity but generally capture lower-quality footage than dedicated cameras or mirrorless options for YouTube production.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/webcams/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/wide-angle-lens/" class="glossary-card-term">Wide-Angle Lens</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera lens that captures a broad view of the scene, essential for vlogging, small studios, travel content, and any situation where the creator needs to show more of the environment from a fixed camera position.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/wide-angle-lens/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/wireless-microphone/" class="glossary-card-term">Wireless Microphone</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A microphone system that transmits audio wirelessly from a clip-on transmitter to a camera or phone receiver, giving creators freedom to move without a cable tethering them to their recording device.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/wireless-microphone/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/xlr/" class="glossary-card-term">XLR</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A professional 3-pin audio connector standard used to carry balanced, high-quality audio signals between microphones, audio interfaces, mixers, and other studio equipment. XLR connections minimize electrical interference over long cable runs.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/xlr/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/xlr-microphone/" class="glossary-card-term">XLR Microphone</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A microphone that outputs audio through an XLR connector, requiring an audio interface or mixer to connect to a computer. XLR microphones generally offer higher audio quality and greater build durability than USB alternatives.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/xlr-microphone/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
          <li class="card">
  <h3><a href="/glossary/zoom-lens/" class="glossary-card-term">Zoom Lens</a></h3>
  <p class="glossary-card-def">A camera lens that changes optical focal length across a stated range, allowing flexible framing without moving the camera or swapping lenses — useful for creators who need to cover multiple shot sizes in one setup.</p>
  <a href="/glossary/zoom-lens/" class="card-cta">Learn more <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 7h8M7 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a>
</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>


